nancial stability despite the freeze on its international assets announced the day before by the United States, the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , Canada and the United Kingdom, in one of the toughest sanctions received by Russia since it began its invasion of Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 These sanctions - which also include the exclusion of some Russian banks from the Swift financial mechanism - paralyze a large part of the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 600 billion euros in gold and foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220228ei2r004ym\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
