\par\par \b \uc2 IronNet Inc\uc2 . - Russian invasion: daily updates of cyber actions to track\b0\par\par\uc2 IronNet Inc. published this content on 25 Feb 2022 and is solely responsible for the information contained herein. Distributed by PUBT, unedited and unaltered, on 25 Feb 2022 21:43:30 UTC. \par \uc2 1,449 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2022\par \uc2 Public Companies News and Documents via PUBT\par \uc2 LCDVP\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022. As included in the Information \par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://docs.publicnow.com/51D098D4C18A3B252D41CD5FF57EDA9C1E0A7D10"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Click here to view this document in its original format }}}\par \par \uc2 Russian invasion: daily updates of cyber actions to track\par \par \uc2 Feb 25, 2022\par \par \uc2 Editor's Note: This blog will be updated by the \uc2 IronNet\uc2  threat research team daily and on weekends.\par \par \uc2 Since November 2021, Russian troops have been building up at the Ukrainian border, worrying many of an imminent invasion as the conflict escalated. Last night, our worries became reality.\par \par \uc2 In a national address, which coincided with a \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  meeting last night, Russian President Putin {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.politico.eu/article/putin-announces-special-military-operation-in-ukraine/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 announced }}}\uc2  that Russia will carry out "a special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in Ukraine in order to "demilitarize and de-Nazify" the country. Shortly after the announcement, Russian forces began to move into Ukrainian territory in a move not seen in Europe since WWII. Russia is now launching a {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/2/24/putin-orders-military-operations-in-eastern-ukraine-as-un-meets"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 full-scale invasion }}}\uc2  of Ukraine by land, air, sea.\par \par \uc2 What we know about the Russian invasion:\par \par \uc2 Political\par \par \uc2 * Russia states that it is ready to negotiate with Ukraine if they surrender.\par \par \uc2 * EU is considering a third round of sanctions targeting Russia's energy and financial sectors ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.consilium.europa.eu/en/meetings/fac/2022/02/25/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 ), including freezing Putin's and PM Lavrov's assets ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-02-25/eu-set-to-freeze-assets-of-russia-s-putin-lavrov-over-ukraine"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * Russian tank in Kherson flies a USSR flag ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Global_Mil_Info/status/1497199339269246982"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * During the national address last night where Putin announced the military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine, he called on Ukrainian soldiers to put down their weapons. He also warned against outside interference, saying: "A couple of words for those who would be tempted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will respond immediately and you will have consequences that you never have had before in your history." * Access a full English transcript of the speech {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://theprint.in/world/full-text-of-vladimir-putins-speech-announcing-special-military-operation-in-ukraine/845714/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 here. }}}\par \par \uc2 * NATO Secretary-General \uc2 Jens Stoltenberg{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.reuters.com/world/europe/nato-has-no-plans-send-troops-into-ukraine-stoltenberg-says-2022-02-24/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states }}}\uc2 NATO\uc2  has no troops inside Ukraine, and there are no plans to send troops into the country.\par \par \uc2 * Western countries including the U.S. and U.K. are {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/russia-sanctions-us-allies-ukraine-invasion-11645670173"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 expected }}}\uc2  to announce additional sanctions against Russia and those involved in the invasion later today (02/24).\par \par \uc2 Economic\par \par \uc2 * Russian gas exports through Ukraine rose 38% on Thursday (2/24) and are expected to increase another 24% on Friday (2/25) ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/business/status/1497149774692298754"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * Russia's billionaires have lost $39 billion in the last 24 hours (2/24) ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.businessinsider.com/russian-billionaires-lose-39-billion-dollars-one-day-ukraine-invasion-2022-2"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * Oil prices have {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/russian-attack-on-ukraine-sends-oil-prices-above-100-a-barrel-for-first-time-since-2014-crash-11645681439#:~:text=A%20global%20oil%20benchmark%20surged,resource%20exports%20from%20the%20region."}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 surged }}}\uc2  over $100 a barrel for first time since 2014.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2022-02-24/ruble-extends-slump-in-offshore-trading-as-ukraine-crisis-grows"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Russian stocks }}}\uc2  fall the most on record, losing more than $250 billion (~45%).\par \par \uc2 * The market cap of Russia's largest bank cut almost in half.\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight{\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2022/feb/24/russian-central-bank-buys-up-roubles-to-avert-stock-market-collapse-invasion-ukraine-fiancial-meltdown"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 has purchased }}}\uc2  billions of roubles to prevent Moscow stock exchange collapse and to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it plunged to an all-time low of 89.60 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Kinetic\par \par \uc2 * Kyiv has entered a defensive phase ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/aletweetsnews/status/1497190487664566287"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * Russian military claims it has taken the Hostomel airport just outside Kyiv and that Kyiv is blocked from the West.\par \par \uc2 * Unconfirmed reports that Russian forces are massing at the Ukrainian-Polish border ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Waheed0819/status/1497198710127611905"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 , {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/JackDetsch/status/1496958617945317377"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * The initial wave of strikes appears to involves cruise missiles, artillery, and airstrikes targeting border guards and military infrastructure, including airbases.\par \par \uc2 * There are various reports of bombings and explosions in multiple Ukrainian cities, including Mariupol, Kramatorsk, Kharkiv, Kyiv, and more.\par \par \uc2 * Russia launched an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.axios.com/russian-invasion-attack-antonov-airport-kyiv-bd1db8ce-757c-4d14-923c-8afa6d43fd41.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 air assault }}}\uc2  against Antonov International Airport (~15 minutes west of Kyiv). Some reports state that they have seized control.\par \par \uc2 * Russian troops are moving on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://apnews.com/article/russia-ukraine-latest-updates-0224-303b0bfdc6148c8738d6ac0ca78142fd"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 three main axes }}}\uc2 : Crimea toward Kherson, Belarus toward Kyiv, and from the northeast toward Kharkiv.\par \par \uc2 * Ukrainian President Zelenskyy {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.washingtonpost.com/politics/russia-attacks-ukraine-as-defiant-putin-warns-us-nato/2022/02/24/e65ea520-9535-11ec-bb31-74fc06c0a3a5_story.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 states }}}\uc2  Russian forces are trying to seize the Chernobyl nuclear plant.\par \par \uc2 Cyber actions the \uc2 IronNet\uc2  threat analyst team is currently tracking\par \par \uc2 Cyber Warfare\par \par \uc2 * Threat actor leaks \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) emails and hashed passwords ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/S0ufi4n3/status/1497143777315758080"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * Ukrainian Military reports Belarusian hackers (UNC1151 / Ghostwriter) are targeting email accounts of military members and using them to send further malicious messages. * Once UNC1151 hackers gained access to an account, they would use the IMAP protocol to download email messages and then use the account's address book to send out new phishing messages to other targets. ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://therecord.media/ukraine-says-belarusian-hackers-are-targeting-its-military-personnel/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * Greynoise has published a list of all IPs that are scanning/attacking Ukrainian IP space ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/Andrew___Morris/status/1496986196874043392"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * The \uc2 hacker group Anonymous\uc2  announced it is officially "in cyber war against the Russian government," stating it has already launched a campaign against Russia and that private organizations will be impacted ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/YourAnonOne/status/1496965766435926039?s=20&t=mks16obUjZcC2kpGaXumfQ"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Link }}}\uc2 ). * Anonymous launched a massive DDoS attack against Russia Today (RT), a Russian state-owned media outlet, which was taken offline by the attack ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.vice.com/en/article/akvy7j/russia-today-suggests-anonymous-took-down-its-site"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Link }}}\uc2 ). * Anonymous posts Ukrainian president's appeal to Russian people for peace to Russian sites ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/DominicNeagle/status/1497201917860143104"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * The Conti ransomware group announced "full support of the Russian government" and that if any entity attacks the Russian government, Conti will retaliate and use all possible resources to strike back at critical infrastructure ( {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cyberscoop.com/conti-ransomware-russia-ukraine-critical-infrastructure/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Link }}}\uc2 ).\par \par \uc2 * On February 23rd, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.zdnet.com/article/ukrainian-govt-sites-banks-disrupted-by-ddos-amid-invasion-fears/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 DDoS attacks }}}\uc2  began targeting the websites of multiple Ukrainian government agencies, including the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, Ministry of Internal Affairs, and the Secret Service of Ukraine, causing outages and making critical government webpages inaccessible.\par \par \uc2 * Also on February 23rd and coinciding with the DDoS attacks, new wiper malware was observed targeting Ukrainian organizations.\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.welivesecurity.com/2022/02/24/hermeticwiper-new-data-wiping-malware-hits-ukraine/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 ESET }}}\uc2  first detected the HermeticWiper malware, which is believed to have been pre-positioned for months. * Compilation timestamp is 2021-12-28. * Attackers gained network access on Dec. 23, 2021. * There has been spillover into neighboring countries, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.scmagazine.com/analysis/apt/ukraine-organizations-hit-by-new-wiper-malware"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reportedly }}}\uc2  impacting organizations in Latvia and Lithuania. * Delivered in one victim organization using previously compromised AD server\par \par \uc2 * U.S. and \uc2 U.K. government\uc2  cybersecurity agencies released an {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.cisa.gov/uscert/ncas/alerts/aa22-054a"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 alert }}}\uc2  on February 23rd detailing the use of a new malware called Cyclops Blink by Russian state-sponsored APT Sandworm.\par \par \uc2 * Avast Threat Labs reported on {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/AvastThreatLabs/status/1496663206634344449?s=20&t=dQgpQVlmhqOgmx5c1PwBsw"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Twitter }}}\uc2  that a new golang-based ransomware is targeting Ukrainian entities.\par \par \uc2 * Kharkiv is suffering significant {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://netblocks.org/reports/internet-disruptions-registered-as-russia-moves-in-on-ukraine-W80p4k8K"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 internet disruption }}}\uc2  (at least 30% drop in network connectivity).\par \par \uc2 * There are scattered {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://twitter.com/ScooterCasterNY/status/1496773671917998080"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reports }}}\uc2  that ATMs are not working in Kyiv.\par \par \uc2 Collective Defense for Cyber\par \par \uc2 At the core of the National Atlantic Treaty Organization (\uc2 NATO\uc2 ) is the notion of {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.nato.int/cps/en/natohq/topics_110496.htm"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 collective defense }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "The principle of collective defense is at the very heart of \uc2 NATO\uc2 's founding treaty. It remains a unique and enduring principle that binds its members together, committing them to protect each other and setting a spirit of solidarity within the Alliance."\par \par \uc2 In warfare that knows no boundaries-cyber warfare-we feel strongly at \uc2 IronNet\uc2  that this concept must extend to cyber defense. For all its promise and prosperity, digital transformation has opened an attack surface akin to a digital infinity pool. Today there is no Atlantic theater or Pacific theater, however. In cyberspace, we are one theater. We must secure it together.\par \par \uc2 Our hearts go out to the citizens of Ukraine as the once-imminent Russian attack became a reality last night. As Putin demonstrated in the 2015 cyber attack on the Ukrainian power grid, there is a potential concomitant war brewing in cyberspace. While critical infrastructure is comparatively well protected, Russia is a nation-state with unlimited resources, a pool of moonlighting cyber criminals, and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ironnet.com/blog/russian-cyber-attack-campaigns-and-actors"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 highly-organized threat groups }}}\uc2  that have been engaging in cyber target practice for years.\par \par \uc2 Long gone are the martial elements of fortresses, foxholes, and field battles. Just as aerial combat changed the very fabric of war during WWII, cyber has forever transformed war as we know (knew) it. In the face of announced and imminently expected sanctions, Putin could turn his eye toward U.S. and European power grids, pipelines, and the financial infrastructure as retribution.\par \par \uc2 It is in this context that the \uc2 IronNet\uc2  threat analyst team is currently tracking the cyber actions noted above.\par \par \uc2 Updates on Russian attack implications on cyber\par \par \uc2 In the spirit of \uc2 IronNet\uc2 's mission, Collective Defense for cybersecurity, we will update this blog with any real-time information we learn about and related threat intelligence. Our goal is to bring together companies and organizations across the private and public sectors to defend as a unified force.\par \par \uc2 About \uc2 Ironnet\par \par \uc2 Founded in 2014 by GEN (Ret.) \uc2 Keith Alexander\uc2 , \uc2 IronNet Cybersecurity\uc2  is a global cybersecurity leader that is revolutionizing how organizations secure their networks by delivering the first-ever Collective Defense platform operating at scale. Employing an extraordinarily high percentage of former NSA cybersecurity operators with offensive and defensive cyber experience, \uc2 IronNet\uc2  integrates deep tradecraft knowledge into its industry-leading products to solve the most challenging cyber problems facing the world today. Follow \uc2 IronNet\uc2  on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and \uc2 LinkedIn\uc2 .\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ironnet.com/blog"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Back to IronNet Blog }}}\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.ironnet.com/blog/russian-invasion-current-cyber-actions-to-track"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Original Link }}}\par \par \uc2 Disclaimer\par \par \uc2 IronNet Inc\uc2 . published this content on 25 February 2022 and is solely responsible for the information contained therein. Distributed by {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.publicnow.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Public }}}\uc2 , unedited and unaltered, on 25 February 2022 21:44:46 UTC.\par \par \uc2 Dokument LCDVP00020220225ei2p00mop\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
