\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Dollar opens sharply lower in Chile and returns to $810 levels on further calm after Ukraine invasion\b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar in Chile opened sharply lower on Friday, in a market that followed closely -although somewhat more calmly than yesterday- the second day of the Russian invasion of Ukraine, which led the United States and other Western countries to decree a series of sanctions that investors were evaluating how they will impact the global scene.\par \par \uc2 The dollar opened down $5.10 to settle at $815.00, after yesterday's jump of almost $30.00, and then deepened its decline by $8.78 to trade at $810.63 before 9am.\par \par \uc2 Despite the initial sharp decline, however, the view from the market is that the unfolding news in Europe will continue to have an impact in the days ahead.\par \par \uc2 "Although today we could see a natural correction after such a strong advance on Thursday, any indication of further attacks by \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Ukrainian soil and/or war \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by other world powers could support a strong advance of the greenback in our country, considering that the dollar has been used as a safe haven \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (for economic support), while emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to show weakness," says Capitaria's head of Trading studies, Ricardo Bustamante.\par \par \uc2 For midday this Friday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  convened an emergency session of the Financial Stability Council (FSB) to address the economic and market implications of the war situation involving Russia and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The instance is chaired by the Treasury and has the participation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Superintendence of Pensions and the Financial Market Commission (CMF).\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220225ei2p0062c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
