\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 VIDEO. Russian all-out offensive in Ukraine: intensified attacks and went for the capital\b0\par\par\uc2 765 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 KIEV and MOSCOW\par \par \uc2 Ukraine decreed this morning a general mobilization to try to stop a total Russian offensive, which in less than 24 hours approached Kiev - explosions had already been heard in the capital -, leaving more than dozens of people dead -many of them civilians- and some 100,000 displaced. Meanwhile, Volodomir Zelenski's government claimed to have killed some 50 Russian soldiers and downed at least 7 planes and helicopters.\par \par \uc2 The invasion provoked in response a reinforcement of Western economic sanctions against Russia, judged insufficient by the Ukrainian president, who regretted that his country has been left "alone" to face the Russian troops.\par \par \uc2 Last night, most of the population in Kiev was taking refuge, while the Government was distributing weapons to resist the Russian advance.\par \par \uc2 U.S. Secretary of State \uc2 Antony Blinken\uc2  said he was "convinced" that Russia will try to overthrow the Ukrainian government and did not rule out that Moscow may try to go further in its attempt to regain influence in neighboring countries.\par \par \uc2 The attacks were air and ground attacks. Russian troops entered from the north, south and east of the country and seized a strategic air base near Kiev, as well as the area of the Chernobyl nuclear power plant, still contaminated by radioactivity from the 1986 nuclear accident, when Ukraine was part of the now dismembered Soviet Union.\par \par \uc2 A STONE'S THROW FROM KIEV\par \par \uc2 The Gostomel air base fell after an attack carried out by soldiers flown in by helicopter from Belarus, a country allied with Russia, witnesses reported.\par \par \uc2 "The helicopters arrived and the fighting started. They were firing with machine guns and grenade launchers," said one of the witnesses, Serguiy Storojouk. That airfield was to be the outpost for launching an offensive on Kiev, which was expected in the early hours of the morning.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Russian Ministry of Defense\uc2  stated that all missions on the first day of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  "were successfully completed".\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  announced the offensive during the early hours of Thursday morning, as reported in yesterday's edition of this newspaper.\par \par \uc2 The Russian military claimed that it destroyed 74 military installations, including 11 airfields, and that separatists in eastern Ukraine are advancing and taking control of territories.\par \par \uc2 Putin, who demands that \uc2 NATO\uc2  close its doors to Ukraine, assured that he does not seek the "occupation" of this former Soviet republic, but "a demilitarization and denazification" of the country and to defend the pro-Russian rebels, whose independence he recognized on Monday.\par \par \uc2 About 100,000 people fled their homes and thousands sought refuge abroad, the \uc2 UN\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Olena Kurilo was injured by glass shattering in her home caused by shelling in Chuguev, near Kharkov. "I will never, under any conditions, surrender to Putin. Better to die," said the 52-year-old teacher, her face covered with bandages.\par \par \uc2 U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced restrictions on exports to Russia and technology imports from Russia, as well as sanctions against Russian banks and tycoons. The \uc2 European Union\uc2  (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) also decided to adopt sanctions with "massive and severe" consequences against Russia. French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  called Putin to "call for an immediate end" to the offensive, the French Presidency said.\par \par \uc2 The invasion has hit international markets. Brent crude oil surpassed $100 per barrel for the first time in seven years and European stock markets plunged yesterday, although Wall Street closed in the green.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ruble, hit an all-time low against the dollar before \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 FALL OF CHERNOBYL\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian government announced the seizure by Russian troops of the Chernobyl nuclear power plant. "After a fierce battle we lost control of the Chernobyl site," said Mikhail Podoliak, chief advisor to President Zelenski's office.\par \par \uc2 Following the loss of control of this area still heavily contaminated by the worst nuclear accident in history, the condition of the plant's facilities, the cover insulating the accident reactor and a repository for nuclear fuel is unknown, the senior official said.\par \par \uc2 "This is one of the biggest threats to Europe today," he said, estimating that the Russians could organize "provocative" activities at the site to blame Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Separately, Russian police detained about 1,400 people in several cities for participating in anti-war demonstrations in Ukraine, according to human rights NGO OVD-info.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  is expected to vote today for a resolution condemning Russia in the strongest possible terms for attacking Ukraine and demanding the immediate withdrawal of all its forces, according to US sources.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220225ei2p0043t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
