\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russian troops intensify attacks against Kiev\b0\par\par\uc2 940 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Russian military forces are trying to advance towards Kiev, the target of missiles on Friday at dawn, according to the Ukrainian government, which denounced attacks against civilians on the second day of this invasion, which has already left more than 100 dead and some 100,000 displaced.\par \par \uc2 The Russian invasion provoked an increase in Western economic sanctions against Russia, judged insufficient by the Ukrainian president, Volodomir Zelenski, who decreed a general mobilization to stop the Russian advance and regretted that his country was "alone" in the face of this offensive.\par \par \uc2 Kiev dawned Friday with two loud explosions in the center of the capital, as AFP journalists could verify. "Horrible shots from Russian missiles over Kiev," Ukrainian Foreign Minister \uc2 Dmytro Kuleba\uc2  denounced on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian military confirmed that it was Russian "missile fire" on the capital and that two of them had been able to be intercepted in mid-flight. The mayor of Kiev, Vitali Klichko, indicated that three people were wounded, one of them in critical condition, in a residential neighborhood.\par \par \uc2 According to Western military sources, Kiev is Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's main target to "decapitate the government" of Ukraine and install a pro-Moscow executive.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, Russian troops entered through northern, southern and eastern Ukraine in an offensive that Zelenski said claimed 137 civilian lives and wounded more than 300 people.\par \par \uc2 "They said civilians were not targeted, but it's another one of their lies (...) Tonight, they started shelling civilian neighborhoods. This reminds us of (the Nazi offensive of) 1941," the Ukrainian president denounced Friday in a video posted on social networks.\par \par \uc2 Zelenski praised Ukrainians for their "heroism" and assured that his troops "do everything possible" to defend the country.\par \par \uc2 "Russia will have to talk to us sooner or later. The way we will be able to stop the fighting and stop the invasion. The sooner this conversation takes place, the smaller the losses will be, including for Russia," he estimated.\par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the Russian army took control of the Chernobyl power plant area, still contaminated by radioactivity from the 1986 nuclear accident, and the Gostomel air base, a strategic point at the gates of Kiev.\par \par \uc2 According to Zelenski, Russian "sabotage groups" have already gained access to the capital, where a curfew is in force. Also, according to the governor of Sumy (northeast), all the municipalities of that region bordering Russia "are surrounded" and "many" Russian armored vehicles were sent towards Kiev.\par \par \uc2 - Refugees fleeing\par \par \uc2 After weeks of increasing tension, with more than 150,000 troops on the borders with Ukraine, Putin decided to begin the invasion of its pro-western neighbor, which immediately came under Russian fire in a large part of its territory.\par \par \uc2 The Russian army assured that it destroyed 74 military installations, including 11 airfields, and that separatists in eastern Ukraine are advancing and taking control of territories.\par \par \uc2 For their part, the Ukrainian armed forces estimated that more than 30 tanks, up to 130 combat vehicles, 7 aircraft and 6 Russian helicopters were neutralized by their forces.\par \par \uc2 Putin, who demands that \uc2 NATO\uc2  closes its doors to Ukraine, assured that he does not seek the "occupation" of this former Soviet republic, but "a demilitarization and denazification" of the country, as well as to defend the pro-Russian rebels, whose independence he recognized on Monday.\par \par \uc2 About 100,000 people fled their homes and thousands sought refuge abroad, the \uc2 UN\uc2  said. Just hours after the start of the invasion, the first Ukrainian refugees were beginning to arrive in Hungary, Romania or Poland.\par \par \uc2 "My life has completely changed in half a day. But it is very good to know that we have somewhere to go," explained Iryna, a 42-year-old woman, who spent the night together with dozens of compatriots at the Przemysl train station in Poland, near the Ukrainian border.\par \par \uc2 In eastern Ukraine, heavy fighting filled civilians with fear and anger.\par \par \uc2 "I will never, under any conditions, surrender to Putin. Better to die," said Olena Kurilo, a 52-year-old teacher, her face covered with bandages, in Chugnev, a town in eastern Ukraine that was shelled.\par \par \uc2 - Sanctions\par \par \uc2 As they had warned for months, the United States, the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , the United Kingdom and other allies such as Japan and Canada decreed sanctions against Moscow.\par \par \uc2 U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced restrictions on exports to and technology imports from Russia, as well as sanctions against Russian banks and tycoons.\par \par \uc2 After a summit of its leaders, the \uc2 EU\uc2  announced measures against the financial sector, energy, transport, exports and visa restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The sanctions package "will increase inflation, accelerate capital outflows and progressively affect the industrial base" of Russia, said the President of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  stressed the importance of the sanctions, but also of "leaving the way open" for an eventual dialogue with the Russian leader, when "the conditions are met".\par \par \uc2 The invasion also hit the international markets: Brent oil surpassed $100 per barrel for the first time in seven years and there were significant setbacks on the stock markets on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ruble, hit an all-time low against the dollar before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Russian invasion also triggered demonstrations around the world, with thousands of people criticizing Putin's decision. There were even protests in Russia, where police detained more than 1,700 people, according to human rights NGO OVD-info.\par \par \uc2 This Friday, Zelenski called on Russians to continue protesting this crackdown. "You heard us and believe us. Fight for us, fight against the war," he said.\par \par \uc2 burs-cat/dbh/bl\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220225ei2p003xi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
