\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia's all-out offensive in Ukraine, decreeing general mobilization\b0\par\par\uc2 938 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Ukraine decreed this Friday a general mobilization to try to stop an all-out Russian offensive that in less than 24 hours approached Kiev, leaving more than 100 dead and some 100,000 displaced.\par \par \uc2 The invasion provoked in response a reinforcement of Western economic sanctions against Russia, judged insufficient by the Ukrainian president, Volodomir Zelenski, who regretted that his country has been left "alone" to confront Russian troops.\par \par \uc2 The general mobilization will affect persons subject to "compulsory military service and reservists" and will be in force for 90 days, said the decree issued by Zelenski.\par \par \uc2 At least 137 people were killed, both civilians and soldiers, and 316 were wounded as a result of the air and ground attacks, he said.\par \par \uc2 Russian troops entered from the north, south and east of the country and seized a strategic air base near Kiev, as well as the area of the Chernobyl power plant, still contaminated by radioactivity from the 1986 nuclear accident, when Ukraine was part of the now dismembered Soviet Union.\par \par \uc2 The Gostomel air base fell after an attack carried by soldiers flown in by helicopter from Belarus, a country allied with Russia, witnesses reported.\par \par \uc2 "The helicopters arrived and the fighting started. They were firing with machine guns and grenade launchers," said one of the witnesses, Serguiy Storojouk.\par \par \uc2 That airfield could serve as an outpost for launching an offensive on Kiev where, according to President Zelenski, Russian "sabotage groups" have already entered.\par \par \uc2 Early Friday morning, the capital woke up again to loud explosions. "Attacks on Kiev with cruise or ballistic missiles resumed," said Ukrainian Deputy Interior Minister Anton Herashchenko.\par \par \uc2 And in the Sumy region (northeast), bordering Russia and not far from Kiev, all municipalities "are surrounded" and "many" Russian armored vehicles marched toward Kiev, its governor Serhiy Zhyvytskiy told the UNIAN agency.\par \par \uc2 - Russia celebrates "success" -\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  stated that all missions on the first day of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  "were successfully completed."\par \par \uc2 President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  announced the offensive during the early hours of Thursday morning.\par \par \uc2 The Russian military claimed that it destroyed 74 military installations, including 11 airfields, and that separatists in eastern Ukraine are advancing and taking control of territories.\par \par \uc2 For its part, the Ukrainian armed forces estimated the damage inflicted on the Russian army at more than 30 tanks, up to 130 combat vehicles, 7 airplanes and 6 helicopters.\par \par \uc2 Putin, who demands that \uc2 NATO\uc2  close its doors to Ukraine, assured that he is not seeking the "occupation" of this former Soviet republic, but "a demilitarization and denazification" of the country and to defend the pro-Russian rebels, whose independence he recognized on Monday.\par \par \uc2 About 100,000 people fled their homes and thousands sought refuge abroad, the \uc2 UN\uc2  said.\par \par \uc2 Olena Kurilo was injured by glass shattering in her home caused by shelling in Chuguev, near Kharkov.\par \par \uc2 "I will never, under any conditions, surrender to Putin. Better to die," said the 52-year-old teacher, her face covered with bandages.\par \par \uc2 - Sanctions -\par \par \uc2 U.S. President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announced restrictions on exports to and technology imports from Russia, as well as sanctions against Russian banks and tycoons. Japan and Canada enacted similar measures against Moscow.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 European Union\uc2  (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) also decided to adopt sanctions with "massive and severe" consequences against Russia that will focus on the financial sector, energy, transport, export control and visa restrictions.\par \par \uc2 The sanctions package "will increase inflation, accelerate capital outflows and progressively affect the industrial base" of Russia, said the President of the \uc2 European Commission\uc2 , \uc2 Ursula von der Leyen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2 , who spoke with Putin during the day to "call for an immediate end" to the offensive, stressed the importance of sanctions, but also of "leaving the way open" for an eventual dialogue with the Russian leader, when "the conditions are met".\par \par \uc2 The invasion has hit the international markets. Brent crude oil surpassed $100 per barrel for the first time in seven years and European stock markets plummeted on Thursday, although Wall Street closed in the green.\par \par \uc2 The Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ruble, hit an all-time low against the dollar before \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 - The fall of Chernobyl -\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian government announced the seizure by Russian troops of the Chernobyl nuclear power plant.\par \par \uc2 "After a fierce battle we lost control of the Chernobyl site," said Mikhail Podoliak, chief advisor to the office of President Volodomir Zelenski.\par \par \uc2 Following the loss of control of this area still heavily contaminated by the worst nuclear accident in history, the state of the plant's facilities, the cover insulating the accident reactor and a nuclear fuel storage tank is unknown, the senior official said.\par \par \uc2 "This is one of the biggest threats to Europe today," he said, estimating that the Russians could organize "provocative" activities at the site to blame Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 International Atomic Energy Agency\uc2  (\uc2 IAEA\uc2 ) called for "the utmost restraint to avoid any action that would endanger the country's nuclear sites."\par \par \uc2 - Protesters detained in Russia -\par \par \uc2 Russian police detained more than 1,700 people in several cities for participating in anti-war demonstrations in Ukraine, according to human rights NGO OVD-info.\par \par \uc2 On the streets of Moscow, there were residents expressing their concern and others their support for Putin.\par \par \uc2 "I'm not happy, I'm very nervous," said Nikita Grushin, a 34-year-old businessman, saying he had no idea who "is right" in this crisis.\par \par \uc2 "I am not going to criticize an order of the supreme commander. If he thinks this is necessary, it must be done," said Ivan, a 32-year-old engineer.\par \par \uc2 burs-cat/bl/mb/js/sag/mar/dbh/gm\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220225ei2p0029w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
