\par\par \b \uc2 Global Equities Roundup: Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,400 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par 19:39\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The latest Market Talks covering Equities. Published exclusively on Dow Jones Newswires throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 1339 ET - The US agricultural economy is expected to have another strong year in 2022, but there are significant factors that could add pressure, says \uc2 Nathan Kauffman\uc2  of the \uc2 Federal Reserve Bank of Kansas City\uc2  . "There are reasons to be optimistic, but there are notable risks," says Kauffman, speaking at the USDA Ag Forum today. Kauffman points out that government payments during the Covid-19 pandemic helped prop up farm incomes, and that support has likely faded as government payments have slowed. Inflationary pressures are also expected to impact farmer incomes, amid higher costs for inputs such as fertilizer. "These costs likely will weigh on profit margins and incomes," says Kauffman. (kirk.maltais@wsj.com; @kirkmaltais)\par \par \uc2 1330 ET - \uc2 Gildan Activewear\uc2  's "blowout" 4Q, according to \uc2 CIBC\uc2  , was driven by strong consumer demand and the benefits from its Back To Basics strategy. Net income totaled $173.9 million, or 89 cents per share, up from $67.4 million, or 34 cents per share, last year. The company's new three-year growth strategy outlines the next phase of growth "as it looks to deliver organic sales growth off an improved cost profile," says \uc2 CIBC\uc2  . With strong demand in North America, the company reported an EBIT margin of 20.2%, surpassing its aspiration of 18%. \uc2 CIBC\uc2  says that Gildan is built on strong fundamentals and is well-positioned to grow its share across end-markets . \uc2 CIBC\uc2  increases its target price on the stock to $49 from $47.(adriano.marchese@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1300 ET - \uc2 Dish Network\uc2  says it's agreed to live with \uc2 T-Mobile\uc2  's planned shutoff of its 3G network on March 31 through a truce now at the desks of DoJ and \uc2 FCC\uc2  regulators. \uc2 T-Mobile\uc2  's planned decommissioning could affect many of \uc2 Dish\uc2  's Boost Mobile customers who still rely on \uc2 T-Mobile\uc2  infrastructure and haven't yet upgraded to a 4G-capable phone. The two companies had tangled over the timing of the shutdown and \uc2 Dish\uc2  secured a three-month reprieve but wasn't able to win further delays. \uc2 Dish\uc2  Chairman \uc2 Charlie Ergen\uc2  says both carriers now share a "good spirit of cooperation," on network issues, though \uc2 Dish\uc2  will keep using \uc2 AT&T\uc2  capacity under an earlier network access agreement. (andrew.fitzgerald@wsj.com; @drewfitzgerald)\par \par \uc2 1254 ET - \uc2 Moderna\uc2  says it has signed advance purchase agreements totaling $19B to supply Covid-19 vaccine doses this year to countries outside the US. But that figure includes no new supply agreements with the \uc2 US government\uc2  . The company is close to fulfilling an older supply agreement with the federal government, CEO \uc2 Stephane Bancel\uc2  tells WSJ. But it's not clear what will happen after that--whether the government will want to sign a new agreement to stockpile more doses for a fall booster campaign, or leave it to private distribution channels and insurers to cover boosters, he says. (peter.loftus@wsj.com; @Loftus)\par \par \uc2 1220 ET - The Russian ruble's depreciation in reaction to the Ukraine crisis is likely to fuel expectations that \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could raise interest rates aggressively in coming months, \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. "USD/RUB may be trading below its early morning highs just below the 90.00 area, but the RUB is the worst performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the world this year," \uc2 Rabobank\uc2  says. USD/RUB rises 7.4% to 87.3706, having earlier reached a record high of 89.9900, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2  . The ruble has pared some of its earlier losses after \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and market participants are likely betting on further rate rises to bolster the ruble, Foley says. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1220 ET - European stocks slump in closing trade as Russia's full-scale military invasion of Ukraine dents market sentiment. The Stoxx Europe 600 falls 3.3%, the FTSE 100 drops 3.9%, the DAX declines 3.9% and the CAC slips 3.8%. Anglo-Russian precious metals mining company \uc2 Polymetal International\uc2  is biggest faller on the Stoxx with its shares plunging 37.8%. European bank stocks also tumble. Energy stocks rise as oil prices jump. "The escalation of tensions arising from the Russian action has pulled the rug from markets, adding to an already brittle environment in the face of rising inflation and interest rate concerns," \uc2 Interactive Investor\uc2  says. (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1219 ET - The \uc2 Federal Trade Commission\uc2  's complaint counsel has filed a notice of appeal in the agency's antitrust case against \uc2 Altria Group\uc2  and \uc2 Juul Labs\uc2  . The FTC sued two years ago to unwind \uc2 Altria\uc2  's 2018 investment in the e-cigarette startup. An administrative law judge last week made a preliminary ruling that the tobacco giant didn't break antitrust laws when \uc2 Altria\uc2  shuttered its own e-cigarette business and took a 35% stake in \uc2 Juul\uc2  . Chief Administrative Law Judge D. Michael Chappell 's decision in the case was made public Thursday. The matter will next go to a vote by the FTC's commissioners. (jennifer.maloney@wsj.com; @maloneyfiles)\par \par \uc2 1153 ET - It is unlikely that Brussels will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to help curb the price of carbon, Jefferies says. Carbon prices in the \uc2 EU\uc2  's Emissions Trading Scheme have surged over the last few weeks to more than EUR90 a metric ton, data from \uc2 Intercontinental Exchange\uc2  shows. This presents challenges for industrial companies and consumers at a time of rising energy costs, Jefferies says, noting that some diplomats met on Monday to discuss measures to curb prices. The likelihood of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains low, as the bloc won't take steps that could be perceived as watering down its climate ambitions, Jefferies says. The measures could lead to much higher prices in the late 2020s when deeper emissions reductions are necessary to meet the bloc's goals, it adds. (maitane.sardon@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1152 ET - Large, late inventory orders are increasingly weighing on corporate balance sheets. Logistics and finance experts say extended shipping delays are tying up importers' cash as they rush to restock depleted inventories, pushing businesses to borrow money and seek other forms of financing. Commercial banking services provider \uc2 US Bancorp\uc2  says its supply-chain finance business balances doubled YoY. Freight forwarder Flexport says its inventory-financing loans more than doubled from 3Q to 4Q last year, and COO Sanne Manders says companies' liquidity needs "are going through the roof" as ocean shipping delays mount. (lydia.oneal@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1146 ET - Coke bottler \uc2 Coca-Cola HBC\uc2  is halting production in Ukraine after Russia launched a military attack on the country. The bottler also does business in Russia. "The safety of our people is our number one priority and we have enacted our contingency plans that include stopping production in the Ukraine, closing our plant and asking colleagues in the country to remain at home and follow local guidance," the bottling company said. "We will keep this under review over the coming days." (jennifer.maloney@wsj.com; @maloneyfiles)\par \par \uc2 1144 ET - \uc2 International Consolidated Airlines Group\uc2  looks likely to report an upturn in fourth-quarter traffic at full-year results Friday Feb. 25, \uc2 UBS\uc2  says. While 3Q traffic was about 43% of the same period in 2019, \uc2 UBS\uc2  says it expects an improvement in the final quarter of the year. It also forecasts 4Q revenues of about EUR3.5 billion, versus the previous year's EUR1.2B and 3Q's total of EUR2.7B, and a pretax loss before interest of EUR306 million against a loss of EUR4.2B a year ago. Still, the shares already reflect market expectations that 2022 is likely to be better than last year, \uc2 UBS\uc2  says.(philip.waller@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1143 ET - The DOJ's move the block \uc2 UnitedHealth Group\uc2  's $7.8B acquisition of \uc2 Change Healthcare\uc2  gets a muted reaction from investors, who were already expecting the antitrust challenge. Change shares, which have recently been changing hands at prices more than 20% below the $25.75 takeover price, edge up 0.8% to $20.40, while \uc2 UnitedHealth\uc2  slips 1.5% amid a lower overall market. The DOJ claims the deal that was unveiled in January 2021 would unlawfully reduce competition. (colin.kellaher@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 24, 2022 13:39 ET (18:39 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020220224ei2o003mp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
