\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Summary: What is going on between Russia and Ukraine?\b0\par\par\uc2 1,163 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  began the invasion of Ukraine early Thursday morning with shelling and ground incursions by Russian troops in several parts of the country, including near the capital Kiev, which have already caused dozens of deaths. The start of the invasion has generated a barrage of international condemnations and reactions. Some 27 members of the \uc2 European Union\uc2  will meet this Thursday and announce new sanctions to pressure and isolate Moscow. For its part, \uc2 NATO\uc2  is planning a meeting by videoconference this Friday. For its part, the United States will submit this Thursday a draft resolution to the \uc2 UN Security Council\uc2  to condemn Russia for this "war".\par \par \uc2  Putin, who for weeks had deployed more than 150,000 military personnel on the borders with Ukraine, crossed a point of no return on Thursday at dawn.\par \par \uc2 "I have taken the decision for a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", declared the President, three days after having recognized the independence of the separatist regions of eastern Ukraine and having obtained the legal framework from the Parliament for a military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Putin assured that he was not seeking "occupation", but "demilitarization and denazification" of Ukraine and to defend pro-Russian rebels in the east of the country. Shortly after his speech explosions began to be heard in several Ukrainian cities, from Kiev to Kharkov, its second city on the border with Russia, but also in Odessa or Mariupol, on the shores of the Black Sea and the Sea of Azov. The Russian army assured that it destroyed 74 Ukrainian military installations, including 11 airfields, and the separatists in eastern Ukraine are advancing and taking control of territories.In Moscow, the Kremlin spokesman, \uc2 Dmitri Peskov\uc2 , affirmed that the offensive will last as long as necessary, depending on its "results" and considered that the majority of Russians will support it.\par \par \uc2 Why did the \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  take place? After decades of tensions between the neighboring countries, which increased in the last weeks due to the presence of troops near the Ukrainian border and the practice of missiles inside Russia, the President of this country, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , ordered a special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Ukrainian territory. The reason is that the Ukrainian territories of Donetsk and Lugansk have declared that they want their independence from the country and consider themselves pro-Russian, so Putin, the President of Russia, recognized them as independent republics and sent troops to their territory on a peaceful mission. Because of this, the Russian Army now has the green light to be in these two regions of the Donbas, where these rebel republics of Ukraine are located, however, the arrival of the troops has been seen as an invasion, which has already caused deaths and structural damage to the territory. Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski on Wednesday called for security guarantees from Western countries and Moscow."Ukraine needs clear and concrete security guarantees, immediately," from both Western countries and Russia, Zelenski told a press conference. "I think Russia should be among the countries that give us those guarantees," he insisted, recalling that he had proposed on several occasions to meet with his counterpart \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  to seek solutions to this crisis.The Ukrainian president thanked his Polish and Lithuanian counterparts for their support and for deliveries of weapons and military equipment."We are united in the conviction that the future of European security is decided at this moment at our home, in Ukraine," Zelenski said.\par \par \uc2 First casualties In Ukraine, the authorities broke off diplomatic relations with Moscow, compared Putin's Russia to Nazi Germany and vowed to defend themselves, while calling for international help to force Moscow to respect the peace.The government announced that more than 40 Ukrainian soldiers and a dozen Ukrainian civilians were killed. In addition, 18 people were killed in a shelling of a military base in a town near the Ukrainian port of Odessa, local authorities reported.Ukrainian border guards also admitted that Russian troops penetrated from Belarus, in a region 150 kilometers north of Kiev, to carry out a Grad missile attack on military targets.There were also other ground incursions from the south in the Crimean peninsula, annexed by Moscow in 2014. Belarus, a Kremlin ally, assured it was not participating in the offensive.Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelenski announced martial law throughout the country, but asked the population not to panic.The president also raised the specter of World War II by comparing the invasion suffered by his country with the 1941 Nazi offensive against Ukraine, then part of the Soviet Union."The Ukrainian forces are fighting fierce battles. The enemy has suffered heavy losses which will be even heavier," he guaranteed, promising to "inflict maximum casualties" on the aggressor.The Ukrainian army claimed to have killed 50 Russian occupants and shot down five planes and a helicopter in the east of the country. All these casualty reports are so far impossible to verify with independent sources.The Ukrainian authorities also closed the airspace to civil aviation for security reasons, while Russia shut down shipping in the Sea of Azov, which connects the two countries.\par \par \uc2 The global economy The situation on the Ukrainian border worsened last week, with violence escalating in the east of the country, the scene of a war since 2014 between the Ukrainian army and pro-Russian separatists that has left more than 14,000 dead.On Monday, after recognizing the independence of the separatist "republics" of Donetsk and Lugansk, Putin questioned the very legitimacy of Ukraine's existence. A day later, the Russian Parliament gave the green light for the deployment of Russian forces in Ukraine.The invasion has hit international markets. Brent crude oil topped $100 per barrel for the first time in seven years and stock markets around the world plummeted on Thursday. The Moscow Stock Exchange, which halted trading for a few hours, suffered losses of more than 30% and the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ruble, hit an all-time low against the dollar before \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Fleeing the war \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  assured that civilians in Ukraine "have nothing to fear", however, in Kiev hundreds of people rushed to the subway to seek shelter or a way out of the city."I woke up to the sound of bombs, packed my bags and fled," said Maria Kashkoska, 29, in a state of shock in the subway.In the middle of the night, traffic in the capital was typical of rush hour. Vehicles full of families were seeking to get out of the city, westward, as far as possible from the Russian border 400 km away.On the roads of eastern Ukraine, the army was omnipresent. A spokesman for the Civil Defense indicated that civilians were being evacuated, but that these \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  were disrupted by gunfire and poor communications.Colombians in Ukraine have reported that mobility is reduced, as many inhabitants of the city look for ways to leave to take shelter from the impending conflict.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220224ei2o0083g\par }\p