\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2 : Dollar advances against rivals after Russian invasion of Ukraine\b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar traded higher against rival \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the market digested the developments of the Russian invasion of Ukraine and responses from Western leaders. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is considered a security asset, so it appreciates in the face of geopolitical conflicts with global impacts. The Russian ruble, on the other hand, has reached the lowest level in history against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 At the end of the afternoon in New York, the euro retreated to US$ 1.1205 and the pound fell to US$ 1.3397, giving traction to the DXY index, which advanced 0.98%, at 97.137 points. The US \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still up at 115.62 Yen at the same time.\par \par \uc2 The DXY index even slowed to a trough this afternoon after US President \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  said he authorized additional sanctions against Russia. According to \uc2 UBS\uc2 , in addition to the support provided by the geopolitical crisis, the US dollar will be favored by expectations of six or seven US interest rate hikes. According to the \uc2 CME Group\uc2 , the market estimates at 86.7% the chances of a 25 basis point interest rate hike in the US at the March monetary policy meeting.\par \par \uc2 For \uc2 Western Union\uc2 , the invasion of Ukraine triggered a slide in risk aversion, causing investors to run for safety in the dollar. "Safe havens like the dollar appear to be in a better position to weather global uncertainty," it said in a report sent to clients.\par \par \uc2 In the early morning hours, in the face of the first news about the attack, the dollar surpassed a historic high against the ruble, reaching 90.0165 rubles. \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced that it will begin \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, as the country has more than $600 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves and gold, an alternative that can be used in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to prop up the ruble. According to Edward Moya of Oanda, the Russian CB has clearly not been successful. "\b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  often fuel excessive movements against what a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to achieve and that is exactly what happened with Russia," he pointed out. By late afternoon in New York, the dollar was bouncing at 85.567 rubles.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220225ei2o000uu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
