\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia's military offensive against Ukraine causes uncertainty among Ecuadorian banana exporters and flower growers\b0\par\par\uc2 1,303 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The start of a 'military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' in Ukraine by Russia, announced by President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  early Thursday morning and which Kiev claims to be a "full-scale invasion", comes at a time when governments around the world are struggling to contain inflation, fueled by the growing demand for inputs due to the global economic reopening after the COVID-19 closures. This situation is already having an impact on the world economy and may soon begin to be felt in the Ecuadorian economy.\par \par \uc2 Russia is the fourth destination of Ecuador's exports, with bananas, shrimp, flowers, fresh fish and coffee being the main products that reach that country.\par \par \uc2 There have been closures and paralyzations of ports and customs in Ukraine in the last hours. One of them is the port of Odessa, which is inoperative, which will complicate the distribution of products, says Richard Salazar, executive director of the Association of Banana Exporters (Acorbanec), who mentions that different shipping companies have announced that they will no longer transport bananas to Ukraine; however, he says that the real effects will begin to be seen from next week.\par \par \uc2 In the case of the flower sector, Ines Ortiz, CEO of Inorflowers, also mentions that the current situation for this export product is complicated.\par \par \uc2 "What is to Ukraine shipments have stopped, what was scheduled to be shipped this weekend and next week, are canceled, even shipments that had already been sent and arrived between Wednesday and Thursday to Holland with which customers are trying to refuse them because of the situation," she says and adds that, along with the tension, there has been a rise in the cost of transport in that region which further darkens the picture.\par \par \uc2 Ortiz says that the atmosphere is one of uncertainty and that it is necessary to wait to see if the markets can be stabilized and that it must also be taken into account that flowers are not a staple product at this time, which can complicate this guild and generate an imbalance.\par \par \uc2 According to figures from the National Association of Producers and Exporters of Flowers of Ecuador (Expoflores) during the months of February and May, for festivities such as Valentine's Day, Women's Day (March 8) and Victory Day (May 9), on average the flower sector allocates $ 70 million to Eurasian countries, equivalent to 40% of its annual sales in these markets.\par \par \uc2 Products for export to Russia 2021The Ecuadorian Federation of Exporters (Fedexpor) issued a statement on the situation in which it mentions that there is a possibility that, if Ukraine receives greater support from Turkey, the passage of the Dardanelles and Bosphorus straits to Russian vessels will be closed, which would return to the most open way to trade with Russia the port of St. Petersburg.\par \par \uc2 The Ecuadorian flower sector allocates $ 70 million to Eurasian countries, equivalent to 40% of its annual sales in these markets, which could be affected by the situation in Ukraine.In the event of a total closure of trade with Ukraine, the sector will stop exporting $ 2.4 million per week, according to the union.\par \par \uc2 However, Salazar says that the situation is not new and that the same could happen as when Russia made the annexation of the Crimean peninsula in 2014 and economic sanctions were established.\par \par \uc2 Among the effects that are going to be registered, Salazar comments that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  devaluation can already be evidenced and that it will generate an increase in the price of bananas that will cause a decrease in the purchase volume, at the same time controls the outflow of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Russia and therefore payment problems.\par \par \uc2 The Russian ruble reached its historical low against the dollar (up to 9 %), before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "As we already experienced at the time, we are going to have collection problems, in 2014 there were between 30 to 35 days of delay", says Salazar and stresses that they also experienced cancellation of contracts due to the low demand that Ecuadorian bananas began to have.\par \par \uc2 Export products to Ukraine 2021Fausto Ortiz, economic expert and former Minister of Finance, agrees that it is necessary to wait and see the size of the conflict and its duration.\par \par \uc2 "As the size grows and more actors become involved, this will take on other dimensions," he says.\par \par \uc2 The expert states that the situation between both countries and the escalation of tension has also been reflected in the prices of commodities such as oil, gold, copper and other raw materials that Ecuador is also exporting, which could lead to an increase in the import of derivatives.\par \par \uc2 The price of a barrel of oil surpassed $ 100 for the first time in more than seven years on Thursday and world stock markets plunged after the launching of the military offensive and gold rose 2.43% to $ 1,955.47 per ounce.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Acorbanec issued a statement and says that "it is urgent and important that the National Government implements compensatory measures to the banana sector that at the close of 2021 reduced its exports by about 4% in monetary terms and 3% in MT according to figures from the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Ecuador\uc2 ". Among these measures they suggest the implementation of the unified simplified refund of taxes for the banana sector, contemplated in article 43 of the Organic Law of Simplification and Tax Progressivity, which awaits its regulation.\par \par \uc2 Salazar also says that other alternative measures could be to pay the producer at the price of the bunch for the fruit that does not come out.\par \par \uc2 The Corporaci\u243\'00\'F3n de Gremios Exportadores del Ecuador (CORDEX) said it has sent a letter to Foreign Minister Juan Carlos Holgu\u237\'00\'EDn, requesting the creation of a public-private working commission to operate as an early warning system.\par \par \uc2 This commission, through coordination between CORDEX and the diplomatic missions to the \uc2 European Union\uc2 , the United States, Russia and China, would allow timely knowledge of the measures taken in the different countries in order to anticipate any inconvenience that may affect the usual performance of exports.\par \par \uc2 Currently, Ecuador exports to Russia an average of 83 products from 504 companies engaged in the agricultural, agro-industrial, aquaculture, fishing and manufacturing sectors. To this destination between 2020 and 2021 about one billion dollars were exported and export growth went from 7% to 9%, according to figures from Fedexpor.\par \par \uc2 Impact at international levelIn\par \par \uc2 its first package of sanctions against Russia, the United States included "total blockades" to two large Russian financial institutions, the Russian military bank and the VEB, the state bank in charge of supporting the development of the economy, managing state debt and pension funds and announced complementary sanctions to hit Russia's sovereign debtAt\par \par \uc2 the same time, the threat of a war unleashed in the last weeks fears about the supply of basic products, such as wheat and metals, in the middle of the reopening of the economies\par \par \uc2 .This Thursday, grain prices broke a record for trading in Europe and wheat rose to a high of 344 euros per ton on the Euronext platform.\par \par \uc2 The price of wheat and corn - of which Ukraine is the world's fourth largest producer - climbed sharply at the opening, a few hours after the offensive.\par \par \uc2 "Russian-Ukrainian tensions lead to a potential demand shock [in Europe] and a larger one in supply for the rest of the world, given the importance of Russia and Ukraine in energy," noted Tamas Strickland of \uc2 National Australia Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 For a \uc2 Swissquote\uc2  analyst, "rising energy prices are a big headache for Europe, because 40% of its natural gas and 30% of its oil come from Russia."\par \par \uc2 As for natural gas, the benchmark market in Europe was 50% higher than the day before. (I)\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220224ei2o00agv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
