\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Markets tremble after Russia's offensive on Ukraine: Wall Street and European stock markets plunge up to 4%.\b0\par\par\uc2 1,536 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  announced a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine to fend off separatists in the east of the country. "I have made a decision on a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Putin declared in an unexpected TV message shortly before 03H00 GMT. In the message he called on the Ukrainian military to "lay down their arms." As expected, markets react in the worst way. Oil skyrocketed to u$s100, gas became 30% more expensive. Stock markets fall up to 4%.\par \par \uc2 Wall Street\par \par \uc2 U.S. stock indexes sink more than 1% on Thursday, led by losses in banking stocks, as a Russian invasion of Ukraine triggered a widespread sell-off in global markets.\par \par \uc2 In the S&P 500, all 11 major sectors traded with losses, with financial stocks plunging 2.9%, while technology and consumer discretionary shares were down more than 1%.\par \par \uc2 Most large lenders, including \uc2 Bank of America Corp\uc2 , \uc2 Citigroup Inc\uc2 , \uc2 Wells Fargo\uc2  and \uc2 Goldman Sachs Group Inc\uc2 , plunge more than 4%. \uc2 Tesla Inc\uc2  fall 2.5% to lead losses among mega-cap papers. \uc2 Apple\uc2  and \uc2 Amazon.com Inc\uc2  give up more than 2%. The CBOE Volatility Index, also known as Wall Street's fear gauge, was trading at 36.81, its highest level since Jan. 24.\par \par \uc2 "While the invasion is not a total surprise, the stock market continues to take a sell first, ask questions later approach," said Ryan Detrick, chief market strategist at \uc2 LPL Financial\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Dow Jones Industrial Average sank 1.92% to 32,495 units, the S&P 500 was down 1.42% to 4,165.23 units, while the Nasdaq Composite lost 0.88% to 12,922 units. The Dow Jones was on track to confirm a correction from its all-time closing high on January 4, settling 12% below its record closing level.\par \par \uc2 Oil\par \par \uc2 The price of a barrel of crude oil surpassed the US$100 mark on Thursday for the first time in more than seven years. Brent North Sea crude oil in its May contract reached u$s101.84 with a jump of almost 9%, while West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude oil traded in the New York futures market in its April contract surpassed u$s100 a barrel with a rise of 8%. Brent crude oil after the escalation of the conflict reached u$s103, its highest level since August 2014. During \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it managed to moderate increases until trading slightly below u$s100 but maintaining the upward trend.\par \par \uc2 Since the tension between both countries began, the cost of the barrel has increased 25%. It must be taken into account that Russia is the second largest oil exporter in the world and this may threaten the world recovery.\par \par \uc2 The level of harshness of the new economic sanctions that are being prepared to stifle the Kremlin economically will be key to gauge how far the rise in energy commodity prices can go. Although \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  pledged not to turn off the gas or crude oil tap - a decision that could change overnight - his credibility is at rock bottom after the attack on Russia.\par \par \uc2 Gas\par \par \uc2 Even more relevant is the rise in gas, with which Russia covers approximately 25% of EU consumption, a share that in the case of oil exceeds 40%. The Dutch market benchmark TTF soared more than 30% compared to Wednesday's close and exceeded 118 euros per megawatt hour (MWh), after touching the 120 euros/MWh barrier in the first minutes of trading.\par \par \uc2 This is a level that gas has not reached since the eve of last Christmas. In just three days, and since Russia recognized the independence of the Ukrainian provinces of Donetsk and Lugansk, the TTF has risen by more than 60%. The Russian attack on Ukraine comes after Germany decided to indefinitely suspend the \uc2 Nord Stream 2\uc2  pipeline license and comes at a time when gas reserves in Europe are at a historically low level of just over 30%.\par \par \uc2 The exponential rise in gas prices over the last year is, together with the increase in the price of CO2 emission rights, mainly responsible for the record electricity prices of the last few months. Each euro increase in the price of this raw material is equivalent to an increase of around two euros in the wholesale electricity market price.\par \par \uc2 Metals\par \par \uc2 Gold prices hit a more than one-and-a-half year high on Thursday and palladium was up 6%, after Russia's invasion of Ukraine raised fears of war in Europe, generating flows into safe-haven assets. Spot gold climbed 0.6% to u$s1,919.30 an ounce after reaching u$s1,973.96, its highest since September 2020. U.S. gold futures gained 0.6% to u$s1,921.\par \par \uc2 "Obviously there is safe haven demand in the (gold) price, but this crisis is very inflationary because it is adding upward pressure on commodity prices (...) it is recessionary also in terms of the growth outlook," said \uc2 Ole Hansen\uc2 , an analyst at \uc2 Saxo Bank\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, palladium was up 6% to u$s2,631.95 an ounce after reaching its highest level since July at u$s2,711.18. Palladium's advance is a natural reaction because Russia is a major supplier of the metal, Hansen said. "The only thing that could counteract it is the risk of a recession, especially in Europe and Germany, which is a big auto producer."\par \par \uc2 Oil prices were soaring and stock markets were falling Thursday as the situation deteriorated. Gold has risen sharply so far in February as the crisis between Russia and Ukraine hit appetite for risk assets. The metal is heading for its best monthly performance since July 2020. Russia is the world's third-largest gold producer, while Moscow-based \uc2 Nornickel\uc2  is also a major producer of palladium and platinum.\par \par \uc2 Among other precious metals, silver gained 0.5% to u$s24.65 an ounce and platinum fell 1.2% to u$s1,079 after climbing to u$s1,126.18.\par \par \uc2 Asian stock markets\par \par \uc2 Major stock market indexes in Hong Kong, mainland China and Taiwan plunged after Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  ordered a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The Hong Kong Stock Exchange benchmark, the Hang Seng, fell by up to 3%. The index that measures the performance of mainland Chinese stocks listed on the Hong Kong stock exchange, the Hang Seng China Enterprises, touched 4.14%. For their part, the two main mainland Chinese stock exchanges, Shanghai and Shenzhen, fell by up to 2%.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock market\par \par \uc2 The Moscow Stock Exchange Index fell more than 50% on Thursday and the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the ruble, reached an all-time low against the dollar after Russia launched a military offensive against Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 The start of the military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  was followed by the suspension of trading on the Moscow Stock Exchange and the St. Petersburg Stock Exchange due to strong volatility in the markets. At 10:00 Moscow time, trading was reopened on the Moscow Stock Exchange. Losses were as high as 50%.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and bonds also plunged, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to announce its first \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  designed to shore up financial stability since 2014, when \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  annexed Crimea from Ukraine. "In the coming days, the Russian market will be extremely volatile. Given the high risks of tightening sanctions against Russia, we are revising our target benchmarks for Russian equities," Evgeny Loktyukhov, Head of Economic and Industrial Analysis at PSB, told Russian media outlet Quote.\par \par \uc2 "There has never been such a significant drop in the recent history of the Russian stock market. The main reason for what is happening is the flight from risks amid the escalating geopolitical aspect," added Vladislav Silaev, a senior trader at Alfa Capital. In his opinion, until diplomats and politicians sit down at the negotiating table, the market will remain in the red.\par \par \uc2 The ruble slid to a record low of u$s89.60 against the dollar and approached a crucial threshold of 100 against the euro. It was around 70 to the dollar and 81 to the euro before the recent round of geopolitical tensions between Moscow and the West began to escalate in October.\par \par \uc2 "To stabilize the situation on the financial market, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  decided to initiate \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the bank said Thursday. The move helped the ruble cut losses slightly.\par \par \uc2 The Moscow and St. Petersburg stock exchanges were forced to halt trading after their main indexes plunged by more than 30%. "Trading on all markets was suspended. The restart will be announced at a later date," the Moscow Stock Exchange said in a statement, reports Efe. The St. Petersburg Stock Exchange, the country's second largest, also announced a "ban on bids and contracts for all trading modes and all types of securities.\par \par \uc2 European stock exchanges\par \par \uc2 At the middle of the session, falls of 4.41% were recorded for Paris, 4.26% for Milan, 2.91% for London and 2.85% for Frankfurt. The Euro Stoxx 50, which groups together the largest capitalization European companies, fell by 3.60%. In addition, the euro fell against the dollar and exchanged at 1.1177 units.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220224ei2o008t7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
