\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Russia attacks Ukraine: Minute by minute after Russian invasion\b0\par\par\uc2 4,003 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Russia today launched a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  against Ukraine, with the alleged aim of pacifying the armed conflict that has been taking place in eastern Ukraine since 2014. This is the minute by minute of everything that has happened in the country. All updates in Central European Time (CET).\par \par \uc2 13:41 Russia nips anti-war demonstration attempts in the bud.\par \par \uc2 "I was detained when I was leaving home," activist Marina Litvinovich, who had called for a protest after learning about the Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine, wrote on Telegram. She confirmed her detention by police in a message to Reuters. Litvinovich had called on Russians to gather in protest in several Russian cities tonight.\par \par \uc2 13:31 \uc2 UNHCR\uc2  calls for keeping borders open for refugees.\par \par \uc2 UN High Commissioner for Refugees\uc2 Filippo Grandi\uc2  called on countries neighboring Ukraine to "keep their borders open to those seeking safety and protection," after Ukrainian citizens have already sought refuge in territories such as Romania, Hungary or Slovakia.\par \par \uc2 "There are no winners in a war, but countless lives will be shattered," the head of the \uc2 UN Refugee Agency\uc2  (\uc2 UNHCR\uc2 ) said in a statement and called for respect for both civilian lives and non-military infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 13:18 "It is an attack on democracy and freedom in the world".\par \par \uc2 British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  said that the Russian offensive "is not just an attack on Ukraine, but on democracy and freedom in Eastern Europe and around the world." In a message to the nation, Johnson promised a "huge package of sanctions" and added that "diplomatically, politically, economically and militarily, this horrific and barbaric action by Putin must end in failure."\par \par \uc2 13:09 Russian troops cross the border in the Kiev region.\par \par \uc2 Russian troops crossed the Vilcha border point in the Kiev region, 50 kilometers from the border with Belarus, the Ukrainian Border Service reported. "Russian troops violated the state border. The enemy's war equipment crossed through the Vilcha border point," the entity reported, according to which the Ukrainian Army put up a battle with the Russian Army.\par \par \uc2 12:40 NATO activates its "defense plans".\par \par \uc2 Europe is facing a new security reality after Russia's invasion of Ukraine, \uc2 NATO\uc2  Secretary General \uc2 Jens Stoltenberg\uc2  said as he confirmed the alliance's decision to activate defense plans aimed at strengthening the defense of member countries in Eastern Europe. "It will be a new Europe after the invasion we saw today," Stoltenberg told a news conference after an emergency meeting of \uc2 NATO\uc2  ministers in Brussels.\par \par \uc2 Stoltenberg said Russia had been planning a "cold-blooded" invasion while \uc2 NATO\uc2  sought a diplomatic solution to the Ukraine crisis and warned that Russia's attack on Ukraine will affect Moscow's relationship with the alliance. "We have no plans to send \uc2 NATO\uc2  troops to Ukraine," the official confirmed in Brussels.\par \par \uc2 12:38 Turkey condemns Russian attack as "a threat to the world."\par \par \uc2 The Turkish government has condemned the Russian invasion of Ukraine as an "unacceptable violation of international law" and a threat to the security of the world. After concluding a session of the Turkish security council, chaired by President Recep \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 , the presidency issued a statement calling the attack "unacceptable" and assuring that Turkey will maintain its support for Ukraine's territorial integrity, sovereignty and political unity.\par \par \uc2 A Foreign Ministry statement also called the invasion "a violation of international law," a "serious threat to the security of the region and the world" and urged Russia to "put an end to this illegal and unjust act as soon as possible."\par \par \uc2 12:35 Ukrainian President compares Russia to "Nazi Germany".\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President Volodimir Zelensky compared the Russian invasion against his country to the actions of "Nazi Germany" during World War II in an appearance broadcast via social networks. "Russia attacked Ukraine in a cowardly and suicidal way, just like Nazi Germany did during World War II," he stated. He also urged Russian citizens to "go out" on the streets to "protest against the war." The Russian president had accused the Kiev government of neo-Nazism in the speech in which he announced the attack.\par \par \uc2 12:22 Moscow: military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  will last as long as it takes\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin affirmed that the military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched against Ukraine will last as long as necessary, depending on its "results" and "relevance", estimating that the Russians will support such an offensive. Russian presidential spokesman Dmitry Peskov told journalists that Moscow's goal is to impose a "neutral status" in Ukraine, a demilitarization and the elimination of "Nazis" in the country.\par \par \uc2 12:19 Costa: \uc2 NATO\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but will have "deterrent" role.\par \par \uc2 "\uc2 NATO\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or act in Ukraine," but will act with a "deterrent" role in neighboring coalition partner countries, said Portuguese Prime Minister \uc2 Ant\u243\'00\'F3nio Costa\uc2  in his first public speech after meeting with the foreign and defense ministers. Costa "vehemently" condemned the Russian offensive and recalled that Portugal is a member of \uc2 NATO\uc2 's rapid reaction group this year and affirmed that Portuguese forces are prepared to place themselves under \uc2 NATO\uc2 's orders in "these deterrence missions".\par \par \uc2 In addition, Costa opened Portugal's doors to Ukrainian citizens leaving the country and announced that instructions have been given to the Portuguese embassies in Ukraine and neighboring countries to speed up the issuance of visas and expedite evacuation processes.\par \par \uc2 12:13 NATO to hold virtual summit on Friday\par \par \uc2 The leaders of the \uc2 North Atlantic Treaty Organization (NATO) \uc2 will hold a summit via videoconference tomorrow, Friday, to discuss the military actions initiated by Russia in Ukraine, diplomatic sources said Thursday (24.02.2022).\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, \uc2 NATO\uc2  announced today in a statement that its member states had decided to take "additional steps" to strengthen "defense across the alliance." "Our measures are preventive, proportionate, and not scalable," the text notes.\par \par \uc2 12:01 \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2 : "This is Putin's war."\par \par \uc2 "There is no justification. This is Putin's war," German Chancellor \uc2 Olaf Scholz\uc2  said at an appearance in Berlin in which he again stressed that the Russian president is "flagrantly violating international law." Scholz joined London and Paris in calling for a \uc2 NATO\uc2  summit.\par \par \uc2 The chancellor advanced that "as a next step" NATO and European Union (\uc2 EU\uc2 ) partners will decide on a package of "tougher" sanctions with which to make it clear to Moscow that it will pay "a bitter price" for the aggression.\par \par \uc2 11:55 Macron calls for \uc2 NATO\uc2  meeting.\par \par \uc2 French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  called for a \uc2 NATO\uc2  summit "as soon as possible" in the wake of the Russian offensive in Ukraine, his office said. The president "wishes the holding of a \uc2 NATO\uc2  summit as soon as possible, in concert with our partners and allies," the Elys\u233\'00\'E9e said, following a similar request from British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 11:45 Lithuania to impose state of emergency after Russian invasion of Ukraine\par \par \uc2 Lithuania, an \uc2 EU\uc2  and \uc2 NATO\uc2  member country, declared that it is going to impose a state of emergency on its territory. "Today I am going to sign a decree to impose a state of emergency," declared Lithuanian President \uc2 Gitanas Nauseda\uc2  after a meeting of the National Defense Council.\par \par \uc2 He also indicated that the country will request the activation of "\uc2 NATO\uc2  Article IV", which allows for emergency consultations if a member of the military alliance is under threat, as other countries have already announced. The ambassadors of \uc2 NATO\uc2 's 30 member countries are scheduled to hold an emergency meeting on Thursday, a spokesman for the military alliance announced, although more and more voices are calling for a summit of leaders.\par \par \uc2 11:26 Germany offers to help with refugees from Ukraine\par \par \uc2 German Interior Minister Nancy Faeser offered support to Eastern European countries, especially Poland, in the face of the expected wave of Ukrainian refugees. The German press estimates that between two hundred thousand and one million people could arrive in the \uc2 European Union\uc2  from Ukraine. "We will offer massive help to the affected countries, especially to our neighbor Poland, if there are strong movements of refugees," he said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 Read: Ukraine closes its airspace to civilian flights\par \par \uc2 Also the governor of Berlin, Franziska Giffey, told local television that the city is preparing for the arrival of refugees. "For the next week, we have set ourselves the goal to discuss concrete implications, what preparations we can make, especially in case people flee this situation," Giffey told rbb.\par \par \uc2 11:22 Ukrainian refugees cross the border to Moldova\par \par \uc2 About two thousand Ukrainian refugees already crossed the border with Moldova after the beginning of the Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Moldovan Interior Minister Anda Revenko reported. "So far we have registered about 1,900 Ukrainian citizens who have crossed the Moldovan border. There are even whole families. Five people applied for asylum," he informed at a press conference, quoted by the Russian agency TASS.\par \par \uc2 For her part, Moldovan President \uc2 Maia Sandu\uc2  assured that her country "will take care" of the refugees and noted an increase in the migration flow at the border crossing points with Ukraine. "We will help people who need our help. At the moment we are ready to receive tens of thousands of people," he added.\par \par \uc2 11:18 United Kingdom calls for emergency \uc2 NATO\uc2  meeting.\par \par \uc2 British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  on Thursday called for an urgent meeting of leaders of \uc2 NATO\uc2  member countries in response to Russia's invasion of Ukraine, which he called a "catastrophe" for Europe. "I call for an urgent meeting of all \uc2 NATO\uc2  leaders as soon as possible," Johnson tweeted, adding that he will address a speech to Britons during the day.\par \par \uc2 11:18 Ukrainian casualty toll rises: 40 soldiers, 10 civilians\par \par \uc2 More than 40 Ukrainian soldiers and a dozen civilians were killed in the first hours of the invasion launched by Russia against the neighboring country, an adviser to the Ukrainian presidency said. "I know that more than 40 servicemen were killed and several dozens were wounded. There are also about ten civilians killed," Oleksiy Arestovich told reporters.\par \par \uc2 Read: Russia defends its attack in Ukraine, says it is not seeking occupation\par \par \uc2 11:05 Moscow says pro-Russian separatists are gaining territory.\par \par \uc2 The Russian Army announced that the pro-Russian separatists in eastern Ukraine it supports are making territorial gains against the Ukrainian army. General Igor Konashenkov, spokesman for the \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2 , said in statements to television that the rebels advanced three kilometers in the Donetsk region and one and a half kilometers in Lugansk, and assured that civilians had "nothing to fear" because Russia has only military objectives.\par \par \uc2 10:43 Ukraine breaks off diplomatic relations with Russia\par \par \uc2 Ukrainian President \uc2 Volodymyr Zelensky\uc2  announced that his country breaks diplomatic relations with Russia after the military aggression against Ukrainian territory ordered by the head of the Kremlin, \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 10:34 Navalni says he is "against this war".\par \par \uc2 Russian opposition leader \uc2 Alexei Navalni\uc2 , who is imprisoned and faces new charges, expressed his opposition to the attack launched by Moscow, which "will cause a large number of casualties, ruin lives and continue the policy of impoverishment of Russian citizens."\par \par \uc2 "I am against this war. I believe that this war between Russia and Ukraine is being waged to cover up the robbery of Russian citizens and divert their attention from the problems inside the country, from the deterioration of the economy," he said at a hearing of the retrial opened against him last week, according to a video posted by the opposition Dojd channel.\par \par \uc2 10:23 Slovakia will also ask \uc2 NATO\uc2  to activate its Article 4.\par \par \uc2 Slovakia, which shares a 97-kilometer border with Ukraine, will ask today at the urgent meeting of the North Atlantic Council to open consultations on Article 4 of the treaty, which applies when one of the alliance countries feels threatened. "The situation demands it," said Foreign Minister \uc2 Ivan Korcok\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In addition to Slovakia, the governments of Poland and the Baltic countries Latvia, Lithuania and Estonia also appealed to \uc2 NATO\uc2 's Article 4, which provides for immediate consultations among allies, while warning against the "foreseeable" Russian disinformation campaign and cyberattacks.\par \par \uc2 10:23 Berlin calls for a strong reaction from the \uc2 G7\uc2 , Europe and \uc2 NATO\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We will coordinate, within the \uc2 EU\uc2 , \uc2 NATO\uc2  and the \uc2 G7\uc2 , to implement the toughest sanctions package," German Foreign Minister \uc2 Annalena Baerbock\uc2  said, warning that these punitive measures will hit the German economy.\par \par \uc2 This war in our neighborhood will have repercussions for us, such as rising prices or falls in the stock markets," she admitted. "But if we do not react with fortitude, the price will be even higher," he added in a formal statement without questions.\par \par \uc2 Baerbock today chaired a virtual conference of \uc2 G7\uc2  foreign ministers - which Germany chairs this year - at which, according to a ministry press release, all members condemned the Russian attack. A meeting of the group's leaders is scheduled for this afternoon.\par \par \uc2 Read: Biden accuses Putin of unjustified attack on Ukraine\par \par \uc2 10:19 Ukraine calls volunteer reservists to arms.\par \par \uc2 Kiev has issued a call to arms to volunteers of the Territorial Defense Units. "Ukraine has entered full defense mode. Anyone who is ready and able to hold a weapon can join the Territorial Defense Units in their region," this military formation announced on its \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page, while giving a list of addresses of all recruitment centers in the country.\par \par \uc2 10:17 \uc2 Council of Europe\uc2  condemns attack and announces measures\par \par \uc2 The Secretary General of the \uc2 Council of Europe\uc2 , \uc2 Marija Pejcinovic Buric\uc2 , condemned the Russian attack on Ukraine, "a flagrant violation of the Statute" of that body, while announcing a meeting of its bodies to "respond to the current situation".\par \par \uc2 "This is a dark hour for Europe and everything it stands for," Pejcinovic said in a statement, in which he pointed out that the armed action is also a violation of the European Convention on Human Rights.\par \par \uc2 10:06 Hundreds of Ukrainians cross the border to take refuge in Romania.\par \par \uc2 "Several hundreds" of Ukrainian citizens crossed in the early hours of Thursday the border separating their country from Romania (over 600 km long) to seek refuge in homes of friends and relatives in the face of the large-scale military invasion activated by Russia, Romanian authorities reported.\par \par \uc2 "The first data from the Border Police show an increase of several hundred people, although many of them have Romanian nationality, relatives or friends and even their own homes in Suceava," the prefect of this Romanian province bordering Ukraine told G4Media.\par \par \uc2 According to some estimates, the Romanian minority in Ukraine numbers about 400,000 people. Romania's Defense Minister Vasile Dincu told the media this week that his government is ready to take in more than half a million refugees from Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 09:57 Russian stock market opens with a 45.2% drop\par \par \uc2 The Russian stock market resumed trading after a temporary halt following the announcement about the start of a Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine with the MOEX index currently down 45.2%. This morning, the Russian MOEX stock index suspended all trading on the trading floor until further notice. European stock exchanges also opened with declines of around 4%.\par \par \uc2 09:49 Belarus does not take part in the Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 Belarus President \uc2 Alexander Lukashenko\uc2  said that his country's troops are not taking part in the "special military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 " launched by Russia in Ukraine. "Today I read: 'About 05.00 a.m. the Ukrainian border in sector of Russia and Belarus was attacked by Russian troops, supported by Belarus.' You scoundrels! Our troops have no participation in this \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," the head of state said at a meeting with military personnel, quoted by the official BELTA agency.\par \par \uc2 09:39 Ukraine denounces entry of Russian tank columns into Lugansk\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Ukrainian Interior Ministry\uc2  denounced the entry of several columns of Russian tanks into the area of the Kiev-controlled Lugansk region in the east of the country. "Russian tank columns entered the Lugansk region near the villages of Krasna Talivka, Milove, Horodysche," the Ministry states on its \uc2 Facebook\uc2  page.\par \par \uc2 09:32 Russia assures that it does not attack Ukrainian cities.\par \par \uc2 "The Russian Armed Forces do not attack Ukrainian cities. There is no threat to the peaceful population," the \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  said in a statement. The Russian military indicated that high-precision weapons are used against Ukrainian military infrastructure, anti-aircraft batteries and air bases.\par \par \uc2 "According to intelligence data, units and servicemen of the Ukrainian Armed Forces leavemassively their positions indicated Defense, which stressed that the places where the Ukrainian forces have laid down their arms are not subjected to attacks. He added that the statements of the Ukrainian side about the losses of aircraft and armored vehicles by the Russian army are a "complete lie".\par \par \uc2 09:28 Ukrainian order to inflict "maximum casualties" on Russian forces.\par \par \uc2 "The supreme commander of the armed forces [President Volodimir Zelensky] has ordered to inflict maximum casualties on the aggressor," said Ukrainian armed forces commanding general Valery Zaluzhni, assuring that the army was "countering with dignity" the enemy's attacks.\par \par \uc2 09:20 Ukraine claims to have recaptured town in Lugansk and killed 50 Russian troops\par \par \uc2 The Ukrainian Center for Strategic Communications and Information Security assured that the Ukrainian Army recaptured the town of Shchastia in the Lugansk region, and annihilated 50 Russian troops. "Shchastia is in our power!" the entity announced on its \uc2 Facebook\uc2  account.\par \par \uc2 09:17 Von der leyen condemns the "barbaric" attack and announces further sanctions.\par \par \uc2 European Commission\uc2  President \uc2 Ursula Von der Leyen\uc2  condemned Russia's "barbaric attack" on Ukraine, announced new European sanctions against Russian "strategic sectors," including blocking its banks from the European market, and warned Moscow that the \uc2 European Union\uc2  will not allow it to "tear down the security architecture" on the continent.\par \par \uc2 "Once again, in the heart of Europe innocent women and men are suffering. We condemn this barbaric attack and the cynical argument to justify it," \uc2 Von der Leyen\uc2  said in a statement to the press alongside the \uc2 European Union\uc2 's high representative for foreign policy, \uc2 Josep Borrell\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "We are in Europe's darkest hours since World War II," said Borrell, for whom the sanctions package they are preparing will be the "most massive and toughest we have ever adopted" and warned Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  that if he does not back down Russia will be "subjected to unprecedented isolation."\par \par \uc2 09:14 Poland asks to activate \uc2 NATO\uc2  Article 4\par \par \uc2 The government in Warsaw called for activating Article 4 of the \uc2 NATO\uc2  treaty, which provides for consultations between members "when, in the opinion of any of them, the territorial integrity, political independence or security of any of the Parties would be threatened."\par \par \uc2 "A moment ago, the (Polish) ambassador (ndlr) in Brussels submitted this request to the \uc2 NATO\uc2  secretary general, with a group of allies," Polish government spokesman \uc2 Piotr M\u252\'00\'FCller\uc2  said. The ambassadors of the 30 member countries of the military alliance are due to meet urgently on Thursday in Brussels, a \uc2 NATO\uc2  spokesman announced.\par \par \uc2 08:50 Moscow closes sea transport between Ukraine and Russia\par \par \uc2 Russia decreed the closure of maritime traffic in the Sea of Azov, which stretches between Russia and Ukraine, following \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 's announcement of an attack on the neighboring country, Russian agencies said. "In connection with the development of anti-terrorist activities, transportation in the Sea of Azov is suspended from 04:00 (02:00 CET) on February 24 until further notice," a representative of the federal maritime traffic agency \uc2 Rosmorrechflot\uc2  told Russian press agencies.\par \par \uc2 Read: Attention: Putin announces Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine\par \par \uc2 08:48 Beijing insists on "keeping calm" despite attack.\par \par \uc2 "China is closely following the latest developments in Ukraine. We call on all parties involved to remain calm to prevent the situation from getting out of control," Foreign Ministry spokeswoman Hua Chunying told a press conference.\par \par \uc2 Hours earlier, the Chinese ambassador to the United Nations, \uc2 Zhang Jun\uc2 , commented before the last meeting of the Security Council that the Asian country believes that "the door to a peaceful solution of the Ukrainian crisis has not yet been completely closed". The ambassador said China's position on "safeguarding the sovereignty and territorial integrity of states" has always been "consistent," but avoided explicitly condemning the Russian attack on Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 08:46 Germany can maintain its supply without Russian gas\par \par \uc2 German Vice Chancellor and Economics Minister \uc2 Robert Habeck\uc2  said that Germany is in a position to secure energy supplies without Russian gas and that one cannot be energetically dependent on a country that violates international law.\par \par \uc2 "We had hoped that it would come to this situation but we knew it could happen and had taken precautions. We cannot be so dependent on a country that violates international law. We are in a position to maintain supply," Habeck told German television.\par \par \uc2 Habeck also referred to the status of the Nord Stream II pipeline - which should transport gas from Russia to Germany via the Baltic - and said he did not see it being able to start operating in the short or medium term. However, he added that in the long term, work must be done to bring Germany back to normal relations with Russia.\par \par \uc2 08:39 France "strongly" condemns war in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 "France strongly condemns Russia's decision to wage war on Ukraine," French President \uc2 Emmanuel Macron\uc2  said Thursday, calling on Moscow to "immediately end its military \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." "France stands in solidarity with Ukraine. It stands by the Ukrainians and acts with its partners and allies to stop the war," the head of state added in two tweets.\par \par \uc2 Macron spoke by telephone with the Ukrainian president, Volodimir Zelenski, who asked him for "unity" of the Europeans in the face of the Russian attack. The French president, who also spoke with the head of the European Council \uc2 Charles Michel\uc2 , expressed "all the support and solidarity of France," the Elysee added.\par \par \uc2 08:48 Ukraine reports at least eight dead and a dozen wounded.\par \par \uc2 "A woman and a child were injured in the Konopot region, where a car burned. In the city of Podolsk of the Odessa region, seven dead, seven wounded and 19 missing as a result of shelling. In the city of Mariupol, Donetsk region, one dead and two wounded," Interior Ministry advisor Anton Geraschenko reported on his Telegram channel.\par \par \uc2 08:39 UK orders its airlines to avoid Ukrainian airspace\par \par \uc2 The UK ordered its airlines to avoid Ukrainian airspace "to keep passengers and crew safe," Transport Minister \uc2 Grant Shapps\uc2  announced. The minister assured that his government "stands with the Ukrainian people and is working with our international partners to respond to this act of aggression".\par \par \uc2 British Prime Minister \uc2 Boris Johnson\uc2  is chairing from 08:30 CET a meeting of his emergency cabinet (COBRA) at which new sanctions against Russia and other measures are expected to be adopted.\par \par \uc2 08:32 \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to halt the ruble's slide\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday announced "\b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to "stabilize the situation" following the start of a Russian military offensive in Ukraine, which triggered falls of up to 10% in the ruble against the dollar. In early morning trading, the ruble was already at an all-time low of 90 rubles to the dollar, down 9.02% from the previous day's close.\par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Russia will ensure the maintenance of financial stability and the continuity of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of financial institutions, using all necessary tools," the institution said, assuring that it had "clear action plans for any scenario."\par \par \uc2 08:30 Russian troops enter Ukraine through Crimea\par \par \uc2 Russian troops entered Ukraine's Kherson region bordering the Crimean peninsula, illegally annexed by Russia in 2014, the Ukrainian Border Guard reported Thursday (24.02.2022). "Currently, movement of military equipment across the peninsula from the administrative border is observed," the Ukrainian entity assured in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The Border Guard Service published a video in which the crossing of armored vehicles, tanks and military trucks through the border crossing point can be seen. The entity noted that Russian forces use artillery and heavy weapons against the border units of the Ukrainian provinces of Lugansk, Sumi, Kharkov, Chernigov and Zhitomir.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220224ei2o006wz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
