\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Stock markets plunge and oil prices rise above $100 after Putin's attack in Ukraine\b0\par\par\uc2 755 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Russia's attack in Ukraine early this morning is causing the markets to tremble. After the generalized collapses in Asia, the main European stock exchanges opened Thursday with declines that in cases such as Germany and Spain have reached more than 4% in the first minutes of trading, while the Russian stock market plunged more than 40% and dragged the ruble down by more than 10%.\par \par \uc2 The fall of the \uc2 Ibex\uc2  35 is close to 2.8% after the initial plunge of 4.5%, with almost all the stocks in the red and falls that are especially significant in the banking sector. Santander (-4.8%), \uc2 BBVA\uc2  (-4.1%), Sabadell (-4%) and \uc2 CaixaBank\uc2  (-3.7%) lead the losses that place the selective in the fight to maintain the level of 8,200 points. The situation is similar in the rest of Europe, where the Dax in Frankfurt and the Cac 30 in Paris dropped 3%, while the Ftse Mib in Milan fell by almost 3.5%.\par \par \uc2 In recent days, the stock markets had avoided the increased tension in Ukraine, which led analysts to believe that investors had discounted a large part of the geopolitical risk in the area. However, Russia's step forward has put panic back into investor sentiment and triggered volatility.\par \par \uc2 "Based on the movement seen at the European open, Ukraine risk was not discounted. Uncertainty will remain in the short term," notes Javier Molina, spokesman for the multi-asset investment platform \uc2 eToro\uc2  in Spain.\par \par \uc2 It was after 4:00 a.m. when Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  announced "a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2 " in the Donbas region following a request for military aid from the self-proclaimed republics of Donetsk and Lugansk and in the middle of the emergency Security Council being held in New York.\par \par \uc2 Then, several explosions shook several Ukrainian cities, Russian troops landed in Odessa and artillery shelling took place on the border following the announcement by the Russian president.\par \par \uc2 In this scenario, Russia has blamed Ukraine for the escalation of the conflict and has defended its decision to launch a military \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the Donbas region before the \uc2 United Nations Security Council\uc2 , which met on Thursday night on an emergency basis.\par \par \uc2 For its part, the \uc2 European Union\uc2  has announced that it will respond with "massive" sanctions to Russia's military aggression against Ukraine, assuring that Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  will "pay" for an "unprecedented" attack.\par \par \uc2 "We expect a sharp drop in equities from current levels. Developed market equities could lose up to 10% in the short term, mainly due to a loss of investor confidence and growth prospects," notes Leonardo Pellandini, equity strategist at Julius Baer.\par \par \uc2 Falling rubleThe fear is most evident in the Russian markets, where both the major indices and the ruble are being hit hard. The Russian stock market has resumed trading after a temporary halt due to Putin's announcement and is down 45% on the MOEX index; since its highs over the last year, the index has plummeted by 54%.\par \par \uc2 The other major index on the Russian trading floor, the dollar-denominated RTS, plunged 41.13% in early trading to 708.86 and is down 63% from its highs.\par \par \uc2 As for the ruble, its decline is verging on 10%, which has forced \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to "stabilize the situation." "With the aim of stabilizing the situation on the financial market, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has decided to begin \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market," the entity announced in a statement reported by the Efe agency.\par \par \uc2 Oil escalationThe economic consequences have not been slow in coming, and in addition to the tension in the stock markets, there is also tension in the energy markets, where oil has soared above 100 dollars in the case of the Brent barrel, the European benchmark. The rise in this case reaches 6% and places the price at 102 greenbacks, its highest value since July 2014, while WTI Texas - benchmark in the US - is placed at 97.29 dollars with a rise of 5.6%.\par \par \uc2 The black gold has been rising steadily for several days on fears that the crisis between Russia and Ukraine could disrupt crude supplies. Russia is the second largest oil exporter after Saudi Arabia, but also the largest producer of natural gas.\par \par \uc2 Analysts believe that the price escalation will continue as the war conflict in Ukraine grows and that it could surpass 120 dollars in its price.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220224ei2o004td\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
