\par\par \b \uc2 Russian Ruble Seen Facing Further Sharp Falls -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 153 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2022\par 10:35\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2022, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 0935 GMT - The Russian ruble faces further significant losses even as \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stabilize market conditions, \uc2 MUFG Bank\uc2  says. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday said it would start \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the ruble hit a record low after \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  launched an invasion of Ukraine. Market participants already expected the bank would need to raise interest rates aggressively before the conflict, \uc2 MUFG\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst \uc2 Lee Hardman\uc2  says in a note. "It is likely that ruble volatility will remain at more extreme levels with the ruble at risk of further sharp sell offs in the days and weeks ahead." USD/RUB rises 5.5% to 85.1960 after hitting a record high of 89.9900 earlier, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 . (renae.dyer@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 24, 2022 04:35 ET (09:35 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020220224ei2o0015u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
