\par\par \b \uc2 GLOBAL MARKETS-Stocks slide, oil jumps as Russia orders troops to Ukraine regions\b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Februar 2022\par 02:32\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2022 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 22 (Reuters) - Oil jumped to a seven-year high, safe-havens rallied and U.S. stock futures dived on Tuesday as Europe's eastern flank stood on the brink of war after Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  ordered troops into breakaway regions of eastern Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude futures rose 1.6% to $96.94, just off their overnight seven year high. S&P 500 futures fell 1.5% and Nasdaq futures fell 2.2%. Asian stocks were also down over half a percent, while Japan's Nikkei skidded sharply.\par \par \uc2 The Russian rouble briefly touched an 18-month low in early Asia trade on Tuesday, after Russia's MOEX equity index had fallen 10.5% the day before.\par \par \uc2 Spot gold, in contrast, hit a new six-month top of $1,911.56.\par \par \uc2 Putin on Monday recognised two breakaway regions in eastern Ukraine as independent and ordered the Russian army to launch what Moscow called a peacekeeping \b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the area, upping the ante in a crisis that could unleash a major war.\par \par \uc2 A Reuters witness saw columns of military vehicles including tanks early Tuesday on the outskirts of Donetsk, the capital of one of two breakaway regions, and Putin signed treaties with leaders of the two breakaway regions giving Russia the right to build military bases.\par \par \uc2 Washington and European capitals condemned the move, vowing new sanctions. Ukraine's foreign minister said he had been assured of a "resolute and united" response from the \uc2 European Union\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 But it was not immediately clear whether the Russian military action would be regarded by the West as the start of a full-scale invasion.\par \par \uc2 Following \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's latest move "we are much closer to military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which of course is going to drive a lot of the risk off sentiment in the markets,\u8221\'20\'1D said Carlos Casanova, senior Asia economist at UBP, adding the short term volatility in markets caused by both geopolitical factors and the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  was 'relentless'.\par \par \uc2 Casanova said the consequences would be higher oil prices, an equity sell off, and people flocking to safe haven assets like the Japanese yen.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's broadest index of Asia Pacific shares outside Japan lost 0.66% in early trade on Tuesday and Japan's Nikkei tumbled 1.6%.\par \par \uc2 In \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, the safe-haven yen rose as much as 0.2% in Asia to a nearly three-week high of 114.50 per dollar, before paring its gains.\par \par \uc2 The euro fell 0.1% to a one-week low of $1.1296\par \par \uc2 "In these circumstances, risk metrics are the driving force," said \uc2 NAB\uc2  head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy, \uc2 Ray Attrill\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The nerves also drove \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  yields lower, with benchmark 10-year Treasury yields diving as much as 5.5 basis points to 1.8715%. Bets on Federal Reserve rate hikes also eased and the chance of a 50-bp hike next month fell below 1-in-5.\par \par \uc2 U.S. policy makers have been sparring publicly about how aggressively to begin tightening.\par \par \uc2 Federal Reserve Governor \uc2 Michelle Bowman\uc2  said on Monday that she will assess incoming economic data over the next three weeks in deciding whether a half percentage point interest rate rise is needed at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's next meeting in March.\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Tom Westbrook in Singapore and Xie Yu in Hong Kong; additional reporting by 