\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Rouble drops to 7-month low vs dollar, Russian stocks down\b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 November 2021\par 10:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Rouble sinks to 7-month low of 75.9225 vs dollar\par \par \uc2 * Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hits two-month low 85.5625 vs euro\par \par \uc2 * Tanking oil prices, geopolitical risks hit Russian assets\par \par \uc2 * New COVID variant also harming risk trade (Updates prices, adds bullets and comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases)\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Marrow and Andrey Ostroukh\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 26 (Reuters) - The rouble dropped over 1% against the U.S. dollar on Friday, cascading to a more than seven-month low as oil prices dived and geopolitical concerns that have buffeted Russian assets all week remained on investors' minds.\par \par \uc2 A global increase in risk aversion related to the detection of a new coronavirus variant also put pressure on the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 After scaling to its strongest level since mid-2020 of 69.21 on Oct. 26, the unit has lost more than 8% of its value against the dollar in a month amid Western concerns over possible Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 By 0855 GMT, the rouble was down 1.4% against the dollar at 75.72, earlier hitting 75.92, its weakest since April 22.\par \par \uc2 "Geopolitical fears have squeezed investors out of Russia funds at a pace unseen since mid-March 2020, while the surge in COVID in the area makes it a perfect storm for Russian stocks, bonds and other financial assets," BCS Global Markets said.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the rouble shed 1.7% to trade at 85.18 , earlier passing the 85.5 mark for the first time since late September.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dismissed concerns over possible military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine and complained about increasing activity in the region by the \uc2 NATO\uc2  military alliance.\par \par \uc2 The rouble's volatility and deteriorating external backdrop may see the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  suspend foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchases as part of the budget rule, said Dmitry Polevoy, head of investment at Locko-Invest.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which did not immediately respond to a request for comment on \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is currently buying around $342 million a day.\par \par \uc2 Promsvyazbank\uc2  analysts suggested in a note that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would end the day trading nearer to 76 versus the greenback.\par \par \uc2 But Otkritie Bank analysts said it looked oversold near 75 against the dollar.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was down 4.2% at $78.80 a barrel, pushing Russian stock indexes towards their lowest level since August.\par \par \uc2 On the stock market, the dollar-denominated RTS index was down 3.6% at 1,606.6 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 2.2% lower at 3,859.5 points.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 75.6820 roubles) (Reporting by Alexander Marrow and Andrey Ostroukh; Editing by Kim Coghill, John Stonestreet and Sherry Jacob-Phillips) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-11-26T10:14:22.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020211126ehbq00x3p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
