\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Russian rouble pares some losses, stocks recovery falters\b0\par\par\uc2 395 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 November 2021\par 14:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap comment)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 25 (Reuters) - The rouble pared some losses on Thursday while a partial recovery on Russian stock indexes, which had fallen sharply on geopolitical fears, appeared to run out of steam.\par \par \uc2 By 1330 GMT, the rouble had gained 0.4% against the dollar to 74.73, retreating from the 75.29 hit on Tuesday, its weakest since mid-2021.\par \par \uc2 Trading activity in Russia is likely to be muted on Thursday, with U.S. markets closed for the Thanksgiving holiday.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has fallen in the past two weeks, weakening from a multi-month peak of 69.21 in late October, coming under selling pressure related to Western concerns over possible Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has dismissed such concerns and has also complained about increasing activity in the region by the \uc2 NATO\uc2  military alliance.\par \par \uc2 "While a conflict with Ukraine is widely deemed unlikely, escalated sabre rattling carries the risk of unintended consequences," BCS Global Markets said.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the rouble strengthened by 0.1% to 83.89 .\par \par \uc2 The rouble still retains fundamental support from Russia's strong current account surplus and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is expected to raise interest rates again at its Dec. 17 board meeting to fight stubbornly high inflation.\par \par \uc2 Non-residents' short positions in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  via \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps on the Russian market were $26 billion on average in November, down from a record high of $30 billion in October, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  First Deputy Governor \uc2 Ksenia Yudaeva\uc2  said on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 When the rouble is weakening, non-residents roll down carry-trade \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a report last month.\par \par \uc2 The Russian Economy Minister warned on Wednesday that the recent drop in the Russian rouble could push 2021 inflation above the previous forecast of 7.4%.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were largely unchanged. The dollar-denominated RTS index gained 0.2% to 1,664.1. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index lost 0.1% to 3,947.7 points, still well off the 3,776.61 level hit on Tuesday, its lowest since early August.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh; additional reporting by Elena Fabrichnaya and Alexander Marrow Editing by David Goodman and Emelia Sithole-Matarise) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-11-25T14:40:35.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020211125ehbp029hd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
