\par\par \b \uc2 Rouble extends losses driven by geopolitical fears\b0\par\par\uc2 387 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2021\par 09:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Nov 12 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble weakened towards 72 to the dollar on Friday, extending losses registered on Thursday on concerns over escalating tensions between Russia and Ukraine.\par \par \uc2 At 0757 GMT the rouble had weakened by 0.4% to 71.89.\par \par \uc2 The overnight decline was triggered by a Bloomberg report saying that U.S. officials had told \uc2 EU\uc2  counterparts about concerns over possible Russian military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in Ukraine, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 "Not helping the \u8216\'20\'18\b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8217\'20\'19 risk trade, geopolitics is again on the radar as the U.S. has flagged its \uc2 European Union\uc2  allies that 'unusual' Russian movements along the Ukrainian border may signal a potential escalation of tension in the region," BCS Global Markets said in a note.\par \par \uc2 The Kremlin has dismissed such concerns, saying that Russia maintains a military presence on its own territory where it considers it necessary.\par \par \uc2 The rouble also came under pressure this week from data showing that inflation in the United States had accelerated to a level not seen for more than 30 years, propping up expectations that monetary tightening could happen sooner rather than later.\par \par \uc2 Higher U.S. interest rates are expected to have a negative impact on emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the rouble is likely to retain support from monetary policy tightening at home.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia is widely expected to raise its key interest rate from 7.5% at its next board meeting on Dec. 17.\par \par \uc2 Russia's strong balance of payments should also help the rouble later this year, said Dmitry Polevoy, head of investment at Locko Invest.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the rouble fell 0.4% to 82.32.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was down 0.7% at $82.27 a barrel, wiping out gains from the previous session as the dollar continued to gain on bets the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will bring forward plans to raise interest rates to tame inflation.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were also down.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index lost 1.8% to 1,820.6 points while the rouble-based MOEX Russian index retreated by 0.8% to 4,156.7 points.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh Editing by David Goodman) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-11-12T09:28:56.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020211112ehbc01cuf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
