\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Rouble weakens as  \highlight22\uc2 Russia \highlight\uc2  readies to step up state  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juli 2021\par 16:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, updates pries)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, July 5 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble weakened in light trade on Monday after the finance ministry said it would increase daily purchases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the coming month, while stock indexes were slightly higher.\par \par \uc2 At 1432 GMT, the rouble was 0.4% weaker against the dollar at 73.51 and shed 0.3% to 87.19 versus the euro .\par \par \uc2 Trading activity was subdued because of a public holiday in the United States.\par \par \uc2 "We believe that \u8211\'20\'13 absent a serious correction in the global stock markets and the oil market, as well as in the current geopolitical environment \u8211\'20\'13 the rouble will remain stable in the current range of 72-74 versus the dollar," BCS Brokerage said.\par \par \uc2 The rouble is set to face more downside pressure from the finance ministry that will increase its daily buying of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for state coffers in July.\par \par \uc2 But the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to see support from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that is widely expected to raise rates again this month, from 5.5%, to rein in inflation.\par \par \uc2 The need to raise interest rates together with an abrupt surge in COVID-19 cases pose challenges for further economic recovery in Russia.\par \par \uc2 "This week's key event is the publication of the Fed's Minutes on Wednesday. Also on the radars is the publication of Russian CPI for June on the same day," \uc2 VTB Capital\uc2  said in a note.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was down 0.2% at $76.01 a barrel after posting gains driven by a disagreement inside OPEC+ about output policy that led to a third day of talks to try to break an impasse among producers in the group.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock lacked momentum.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was up 0.07% to 1,660.8 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 0.3% higher at 3,875.8 points.\par \par \uc2 Shares in Russian sparkling wine maker \uc2 Abrau-Durso\uc2  outperformed the market by gaining 4.3% on the day after new legislation forced foreign champagne producers to add a "sparkling wine" reference to the back of their bottles.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh; Editing by Angus MacSwan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-7-5T15:47:08.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210705eh75028k1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
