\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Global  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2 : dollar trades lower against most  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 442 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 April 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell on Thursday against major rivals, with data publishing in the United States that raised risk appetite. U.S. assets also followed the treasuries' yield movement, which retreated today. The momentum benefited much of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of emerging countries, especially Turkey, whose \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  today maintained the basic interest rate. Contrary to the trend, the ruble devalued itself, in a session marked by US sanctions on Russia.\par \par \uc2 The DXY index, which is about the dollar against six rival \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fell 0.01 percent to 91.684 points in late afternoon in NEW YORK. The euro, in turn, depreciated to $1.1973 in the late afternoon, limiting DXY losses. The pound was trading higher against the dollar at $1.3789. Against the yen, the dollar fell to 108.69 yen.\par \par \uc2 "The dollar struggled to recover today despite strong U.S. economic reports," BK Asset said. The country's retail sales jumped 9.8% in March compared to February, well above analysts' expectations. Applications for unemployment benefits fell to 576,000, well below the expectation of 710,000. The "positive data" should have boosted the dollar, but there were very few buyers. Instead, the dollar followed lower Treasuries yields," says the asset manager.\par \par \uc2 "While impressive, the data released today does little to lower the \uc2 Federal Reserve\uc2 's high standard for changing the course of a highly accommodative policy," says Western Union market analyst Joe Manimbo. The euro, in turn, did not capitalize on the movement. The "coronavirus vaccination campaign in Europe will delay the economic recovery of the euro zone, which will have resumed late compared to the United Kingdom and the United States," \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  said in a report.\par \par \uc2 In the first monetary policy decision since President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in authority, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Turkey\uc2  (CBRT) today announced the maintenance of the country's basic interest rate at 19% \u8211\'20\'13 thus interrupting the cycle of interest rates that bothered the head of the local executive. By the end of the afternoon, the dollar depreciated to 8.0068 lire.\par \par \uc2 The ruble contradicted most emerging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and weakened sharply after Washington announced the imposition of a series of new sanctions against \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  over Moscow's alleged \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the U.S. elections. In the late afternoon in NY, the dollar was valued at 76.373 rubles. The Argentine peso also reversed trend, amid the escalation of covid-19 and the announcement of price restrictions in the country, following the highest inflation in 18 months, published today. The dollar was valued at 92.7552 pesos at the same time.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020210416eh4f000e3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
