\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Rouble hits one-month high vs dollar as Russia leaves rates unchanged\b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Oktober 2020\par 16:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Rouble hits one-month high against the dollar\par \par \uc2 * C.bank keeps key rate at record low of 4.25%\par \par \uc2 * Additional c.bank \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales to start on Oct. 26 (Updates prices, adds \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales detail)\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Marrow and Andrey Ostroukh\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Oct 23 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble gained on Friday, reaching a one-month peak against the dollar as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left interest rates unchanged at 4.25%, with optimism over U.S. stimulus measures boosting riskier assets.\par \par \uc2 By 1433 GMT the rouble was 0.4% stronger against the dollar at 76.28, after earlier touching 76.12, its strongest since Sept. 22.\par \par \uc2 Versus the euro, the rouble was up 0.3% to 90.23 , having earlier hit a near one-month high of 90.15.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to keep rates at a record low came in line with expectations that Russia would opt to keep the cost of lending unchanged amid increased global market volatility.\par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said a rate cut was still possible in the coming months.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Elvira Nabiullina\uc2 , presenting the rate decision, said her bank will next week start extra foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales related to Russia's decision to buy more shares in its flagship air carrier \uc2 Aeroflot\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 From Oct. 26, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase to the equivalent of 9.8 billion roubles ($128.3 million) from around 8.7 billion roubles currently, according to Reuters calculations.\par \par \uc2 U.S INFLUENCE\par \par \uc2 Since hitting a six-month low in late September, the rouble has weathered a series of geopolitical risks, including sanctions on top Russian officials, a political crisis in Belarus and a military conflict in the South Caucasus.\par \par \uc2 Investors are now focused on what the outcome of the U.S. presidential election on Nov. 3 might mean for the Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "A (Joe) Biden U.S. presidential victory is gaining momentum, elevating speculation that Washington will take a harder line with Moscow," said BCS Global Markets in a note.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was down 0.3% at $42.35 a barrel. President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  on Thursday hinted that Russia could extend oil output cuts should the situation warrant it.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were up. The dollar-denominated RTS index rose 0.8% to 1,164.1 points, while the rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 0.6% higher at 2,818.6 points.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see ($1 = 76.3640 roubles) (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh and Alexander Marrow; Additional reporting by Elena Fabrichnaya; Editing by Larry King and Jan Harvey) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-10-23T15:42:13.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201023egan01zu6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
