\par\par \b \uc2 Analysis: Biden risk looms for Turkey's Erdogan and beleaguered lira\b0\par\par\uc2 949 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Oktober 2020\par 13:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 ISTANBUL (Reuters) - Turkey stands to lose more than most other countries if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is elected president since he is expected to toughen the U.S. stance against President \uc2 Tayyip Erdogan\uc2 's foreign military \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and closer cooperation with \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Investors and analysts say the beleaguered Turkish lira is especially vulnerable if a Biden White House pulls the trigger on long-threatened sanctions over Ankara's purchase of Russian S-400 missiles, which Washington says compromise \uc2 NATO\uc2  defences.\par \par \uc2 An apparent S-400s test last week prompted a furious response from the State Department and Pentagon. Top Republican and Democratic U.S. senators also called for sanctions that could hobble a Turkish economy hit by two slumps in as many years.\par \par \uc2 Erdogan has downplayed possible fallout and promised counter-sanctions.\par \par \uc2 The American threats have rung hollow since Moscow shipped the weapons to Ankara in mid-2019, largely because President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  has resisted punishing Erdogan, with whom he has regular calls, saying he hopes talks will resolve the issue.\par \par \uc2 Erdogan has leveraged his warm ties with Trump to flex military muscle in Syria, Libya, the Eastern Mediterranean and this month in Nagorno-Karabakh, filling some gaps left by a U.S. retreat from the region in recent years.\par \par \uc2 But the relationship could cool if Biden, the Democratic candidate and front-runner, wins the November 4 election.\par \par \uc2 In remarks that drew sharp criticism from Ankara, Biden in December advocated a new approach to the "autocrat" Erdogan and fretted over close Turkish cooperation with Russia.\par \par \uc2 Biden has said little specifically about the issue recently and his campaign did not respond to a request to comment. His platform calls on "all \uc2 NATO\uc2  nations to recommit to their responsibilities as members of a democratic alliance."\par \par \uc2 The lira, down 24% this year to all-time lows, already partly reflects the Biden risk, investors say. Any decisive rebound in Turkish assets may be delayed until after the vote when the White House decides whether, and perhaps how, to sanction Turkey.\par \par \uc2 "A Biden victory would certainly increase the risk of U.S. sanctions ... and of course you'll have anxiety returning to an already unstable financial market that has been hit by the pandemic," said Roger Kelly, lead regional economist at the European Bank for Reconstruction and Development.\par \par \uc2 The lira's slide is due mostly to depleted \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , double-digit inflation and what \uc2 Moody's\uc2  says is a balance-of-payments risk.\par \par \uc2 Yet the U.S. election has loomed in the background: the latest \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selloff began in July, when Biden's near 10-point lead in polls solidified. A Turkish government spokesperson did not immediately respond to a request for comment.\par \par \uc2 For a graphic on Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  split by U.S. election risk:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/mkt/dgkpljmelpb/Pasted%20image%201602583295562.png"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/mkt/dgkpljmelpb/Pasted%20image%201602583295562.png}}}\par \par \uc2 Some investors say now that $13.5 billion has been pulled from Turkish bonds and stocks this year there's good reason to invest, especially after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began hiking its key interest rate, which is expected to hit 12% on Thursday.\par \par \uc2 But sanctions over S-400s, now back on the radar, are making some optimists think twice.\par \par \uc2 "There's justification for owning Turkish hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  paper. You may have to navigate through some choppiness but ... quite a bit of bad news is already priced in," said Blaise Antin, head of EM sovereign research at Los Angeles-based TCW.\par \par \uc2 "Yet the Erdogan back channel to the White House will very likely be much weaker" under Biden, he added. "Erdogan is a pragmatic guy. I expect he would try some sort of pivot."\par \par \uc2 NEW U.S. APPROACH\par \par \uc2 Turkey's Presidential Spokesman \uc2 Ibrahim Kalin\uc2  said this month it would work with any U.S. president yet press him to abandon support for Kurdish militant groups in Syria, and to extradite U.S.-based Muslim cleric Fethullah Gulen who it says orchestrated a failed coup in 2016.\par \par \uc2 Finance Minister \uc2 Berat Albayrak\uc2  has downplayed the fall in the lira, which is near 8 versus the dollar, and he expects Turkey's economy to avoid a contraction this year.\par \par \uc2 For a graphic on Timeline of Turkish lira's gradual decline:\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/mkt/yxmvjjnyqvr/Lira%20timeline%20US%20elections.PNG"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/mkt/yxmvjjnyqvr/Lira%20timeline%20US%20elections.PNG}}}\par \par \uc2 Foreign holdings of Turkish government debt have fallen to 3% from more than 25% five years ago. Flows briefly reversed after last month's surprise rate hike, but the rally was cut short by reports of the planned S-400 test.\par \par \uc2 A U.S. House defence spending bill worth hundreds of billions of dollars includes sanctions on Turkey under the Countering America's Adversaries Through Sanctions Act (CAATSA) that is meant to punish countries dealing with Russia.\par \par \uc2 The Senate could pass it and send it to the White House as soon as December, setting the stage for Biden or Trump to select mild or harsh sanctions next year. Separately last year, Washington suspended Ankara's involvement in an F-35 programme.\par \par \uc2 Erdogan sees Turkey's \uc2 NATO\uc2  membership and its opposition to Russia in conflicts in both Syria and Libya as a check on what any U.S. Administration might do, said Nikolay Markov, senior economist at Pictet Asset Management.\par \par \uc2 "The U.S. will need to rely on Turkey as the main ally in that region, so that puts a cap on sanctions they can take against Turkey," he said.\par \par \uc2 (For a lira timeline, click here: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://tmsnrt.rs/3dR1RCY"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://tmsnrt.rs/3dR1RCY}}}\uc2 )\par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by Rodrigo Campos in New York, Nevzat Devranoglu in Ankara and Tom Arnold in London; edited by Philippa Fletcher) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-10-21T11:23:15.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020201021egal01n6l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
