\par\par \b \uc2 Rouble hits 93 vs euro as conflict risk pummels Russian assets\b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 September 2020\par 09:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, Sept 29 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble nosedived on Tuesday, hitting 93 against the euro and continuing its sharp downward trajectory from the previous two trading sessions as clashes in Nagorno-Karabakh and rising coronavirus cases at home weighed on Russian assets.\par \par \uc2 At 0732 GMT, the rouble had lost 0.8% to trade at 93.04 versus the euro, reaching levels not seen since January 2016.\par \par \uc2 It was 0.8% weaker against the dollar at 79.70 , earlier hitting 79.8725 for the first time since March 30.\par \par \uc2 Fighting escalated on Monday between Russia's neighbour Azerbaijan and its ethnic Armenian mountain enclave of Nagorno-Karabakh, and at least 55 people were killed in a second day of heavy clashes, with more casualties reported overnight.\par \par \uc2 The main reason for pressure on rouble assets was investors' fears that Russia would be dragged into the conflict, said Alor Broker analyst Alexei Antonov. He added that the spread of coronavirus in Russia was another risk.\par \par \uc2 Moscow school holidays in October will be extended, while sources told Reuters last week that hospitals have been instructed to free up hundreds of beds for COVID-19 patients in the capital, in response to a sharp increase in cases.\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday said it would sell an additional 2.9 billion roubles a day as part of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , starting from Oct. 1. It has been carrying out foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since March.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main export, was down 0.2% at $42.27 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were mixed.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was down 0.5% to 1,161.5 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 0.3% higher at 2,937.0 points.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 (Reporting by Alexander Marrow; Editing by Kirsten Donovan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-9-29T08:42:43.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200929eg9t013l3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
