\par\par \b \uc2 EMERGING MARKETS- \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  rally after Fed shift; Russian rouble up with eyes on Kremlin\b0\par\par\uc2 511 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 August 2020\par 10:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 * Fed signals lower interest rate environment for longer\par \par \uc2 * Rouble firms; Moscow defies calls to probe Navalny illness\par \par \uc2 * Kremlin says police force for Belarus to be deployed if needed\par \par \uc2 * Turkey's lira rises but inflation and Greece tensions persist\par \par \uc2 By Susan Mathew\par \par \uc2 Aug 28 (Reuters) - An index of emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit its highest in nearly six months as the dollar slid after the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 's new strategy, while Russia's rouble firmed with eyes on the Kremlin after Belarus' leader sought help amid protests.\par \par \uc2 Fed Chair \uc2 Jerome Powell\uc2  unveiled a new monetary policy strategy which pledged to address "shortfalls" from the "broad-based and inclusive goal" of full employment, and less on worries about too-high inflation, signalling lower interest rates for longer.\par \par \uc2 EM stocks hovered near seven-month highs, although a rally in most Asian shares failed to carry over as equities in emerging Europe, Middle East and Africa tracked a lower open on the western European bourses.\par \par \uc2 MSCI's index of developing market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose 0.2% as the greenback slid against major rivals, with lower U.S. interest rate environment supporting rate differentials with the higher-yielding emerging markets.\par \par \uc2 Russia's rouble looked to end a tumultuous week about 0.3% higher. On request from Belarusian leader \uc2 Alexander Lukashenko\uc2 , the Kremlin set up a police force to be deployed only if unrest spun out of control in the ex-Soviet nation.\par \par \uc2 The Kermlin's comments "do not remove a tail risk of a potential \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (that we consider the biggest risk for the Russian assets) but more like a hope that protesters' moves will be exhausted on their own," said Credit Suisse analyst Alexey Pogorelov.\par \par \uc2 Amid concerns about ties with the West, the Kremlin also defied calls from Germany, the United States and other powers to investigate the suspected poisoning of opposition leader \uc2 Alexei Navalny\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Political uncertainty seemed to be the theme of the day with Japanese Prime Minister \uc2 Shinzo Abe\uc2  set to resign for health reasons later, while in Romania, the opposition said they have enough votes to topple the cabinet in a no-confidence vote scheduled for Monday.\par \par \uc2 Romania's leu traded flat, sitting out the rally in riskier \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Commerzbank \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Elisabeth Andreae said it seemed likely that Prime Minister \uc2 Ludovic Orban\uc2 's government will continue governing until elections in December in which case it should have little impact on the leu.\par \par \uc2 South Africa's rand rose 0.9%, while gains in Turkey's lira were limited after minutes of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's last meeting showed indications of a sustained rise in inflation.\par \par \uc2 Ahead of GDP data next week, a Reuters poll showed Turkey's economy may have contracted nearly 12% in the second quarter due to the coronavirus lockdown. Flare-up in tensions with Greece regarding energy resources in the Mediterranean were also being watched for. (Reporting by Susan Mathew in Bengaluru; editing by Uttaresh.V) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-8-28T09:18:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200828eg8s01b2i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
