\par\par \b \uc2 Russian c.bank will not make  \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions \highlight\uc2  on June 24, July 1\b0\par\par\uc2 150 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2020\par 09:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, June 5 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday said it would not conduct foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  on June 24 or July 1 as those days have now been made public holidays.\par \par \uc2 It has been carrying out \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales since early March, its first such \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in five years, to support the rouble, which was hit by the spread of the novel coronavirus and sliding oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which reveals the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales with a two-day lag, on Friday said it had sold 11.3 billion roubles ($164.6 million) worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 The Moscow Exchange has said that trading will not be conducted on those days. ($1 = 68.6700 roubles) (Reporting by Alexander Marrow and Elena Fabrichnaya; Editing by Kevin Liffey) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-6-5T08:28:44.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200605eg650129t\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
