\par\par \b \uc2 Russian  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  scales back  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2  as oil recovers\b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 2020\par 13:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, May 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reduced the amount of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  it sells on the market to support the rouble as the price of oil - a key export - has risen, data showed on Friday.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  began selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from state reserves in March for the first time since early 2015 as the rouble slid to four-year lows amid a crash in oil prices and the global spread of the novel coronavirus.\par \par \uc2 Since Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has only been carrying out regular foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales, within budget rules. It has stopped additional sales related to the price of Urals, Russia's blend of crude oil <URL-E>, which has recovered a little after tumbling below $25 per barrel.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which reports its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales with a two-day lag, said on Friday it sold 11.4 billion roubles ($155 million) worth of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday, down from around 20 billion roubles in early May.\par \par \uc2 "In the absence of stable demand for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from local businesses, this is enough to maintain a balance for now," said Dmitry Polevoy, chief economist at the \uc2 Russian Direct Investment Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Oil prices have steadily increased this month as lockdown restrictions around the world gradually begin to be eased, with previously shuttered economies sputtering back into life.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of Russia, which let the rouble float freely in late 2014, uses two formulas to determine the level of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales, which, it says, are aimed at reducing volatility and the financial risks it bears.\par \par \uc2 It sells foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under Russia's fiscal rule when prices for Urals fall below $42 per barrel, the threshold crossed on March 3.\par \par \uc2 Another mechanism, related to the government's deal to purchase the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stake in lender \uc2 Sberbank\uc2 , allows extra foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling when Urals prices fall below $25 to compensate for the shortfall of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  conversions from the revenue of export-focused companies.\par \par \uc2 The lower the oil price, the larger the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Urals prices fell below $25 on March 18, triggering the second mechanism, but have held above that since May 7. On Friday, the price reached almost $31 for the first time in two months.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has repeatedly said it does not target a specific rouble exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 73.5400 roubles) (Reporting by Elena Fabrichnaya, Additional reporting by Vladimir Abramov; Writing Alexander Marrow; Editing by Mark Potter) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-15T12:59:23.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200515eg5f01q9p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
