\par\par \b \uc2 Rouble firms ahead of state  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  sales data,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  media conference\b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Mai 2020\par 10:21\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, May 8 (Reuters) - The rouble firmed slightly in early trade on Friday, ahead of the publication of the finance ministry's plan for state foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling for the month ahead and a media conference with the head of the \uc2 Russian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 0752 GMT, the rouble was 0.4% firmer against the dollar at 73.82 and against the euro gained 0.4% to trade at 79.95.\par \par \uc2 Russia is expected to more than double its foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling from state reserves to $2.5 billion in May, according to a Reuters survey. The finance ministry will announce details at 0900 GMT. The ministry has a selling plan for the month ahead which is carried out by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on a daily basis.\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 18.6 billion roubles ($252.13 million) worth of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the rouble, in \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  that include the finance ministry's selling plan and extra \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  when prices for \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Urals crude blend slip below $25 per barrel.\par \par \uc2 "The current balance of market flows is relatively favourable for the rouble," said Dmitry Polevoy, chief economist at the \uc2 Russian Direct Investment Fund\uc2 .\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor \uc2 Elvira Nabiullina\uc2  will hold a weekly online media conference at 1200 GMT where she is expected to shed more light on the bank's plan to cut rates to support the economy, hit by the coronavirus outbreak.\par \par \uc2 Consumer inflation in Russia accelerated to 3.1% in April, in line with market expectations, which should not impede further cuts to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key rate, now at 5.5%, \uc2 Nordea Bank\uc2  analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Market volatility may increase later on Friday ahead of Russia's long weekend to commemorate Victory day. The Moscow Exchange will be closed for three days until May 12, which usually prompts investors to minimise risk-taking.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was down 0.5% to 1,120.4 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 0.4% lower at 2,624.2 points.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see ($1 = 73.7725 roubles) (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh. Editing by Jane Merriman) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-8T09:21:00.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200508eg58017d9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
