\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Rouble slips in expectation of reduced  \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 371 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Mai 2020\par 14:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Adds detail, updates prices)\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, May 6 (Reuters) - The rouble weakened on Wednesday as the market priced in a likely decline in \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  amid a recovery in prices for oil, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key exports.\par \par \uc2 At 1254 GMT, the rouble was down 1% against the dollar at 74.51, heading towards 81.97, its weakest level since early 2016, which it reached in March as oil prices crashed and the new coronavirus spread.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has lost more than 16% against the dollar so far this year and has been supported since March by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the first in nearly five years.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  selling volumes are pegged to oil prices. If prices for crude go up, the bank reduces the amount of daily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 On Wednesday, prices for Urals, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's blend of crude <URL-E>, rose above the $25 threshold, suggesting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reduced \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which it reports with a two-day lag.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it had sold 20.2 billion roubles ($272 million) worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  on April 29, before Russia's May holidays began.\par \par \uc2 Versus the euro, the rouble shed 0.9% of its value to 80.63 .\par \par \uc2 The market keeps an eye of President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 , who is expected to shed light on Russia's plans to fight the novel coronavirus, particularly the scope for lifting the virus-related lockdowns that have suffocated economic activity.\par \par \uc2 Russia has reported 165,929 cases of the virus and 1,537 coronavirus-related deaths.\par \par \uc2 Prices for Brent crude oil, a global benchmark, were down 0.7% to $30.74, having climbed 13.9% in the previous session on hopes for a recovery in demand as some countries ease coronavirus lockdowns.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were mixed. The dollar-denominated RTS index was down 1.3% to 1,118.9 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was flat at 2,653.8 points.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see ($1 = 74.2200 roubles) (Reporting by Gabrielle T\u233\'00\'E9trault-Farber and Andrey Ostroukh; editing by Larry King) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-6T13:25:10.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200506eg56020at\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
