\par\par \b \uc2 Rouble firms past 74 vs dollar as oil prices recover\b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Mai 2020\par 09:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, May 5 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble firmed in light trade on Tuesday, supported by a recovery in prices for oil, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key export, in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 At 0707 GMT, the rouble was 1.2% stronger against the dollar at 73.95, heading away from the 75.97 hit briefly on Monday which was the weakest level since April 22.\par \par \uc2 Versus the euro, the rouble firmed 1.3% to 80.57 .\par \par \uc2 Market volatility could be higher than usual and trading activity below average as Monday and Tuesday are official holidays in Russia.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, investors priced in an increase in oil prices driven by expectations that fuel demand will begin to recover as some U.S. states and nations in Europe and Asia start to ease coronavirus lockdown measures.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was up 7.2% at $29.14 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 The rouble, however, received no support from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Monday and Tuesday, but it is expected to resume daily selling of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling around $270 million worth of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day to ease downside pressure on the rouble in the first \b \highlight22\uc2 FX interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2015.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes rose.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was up 2.7% to 1,128.9 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 1.1% higher at 2,653.6 points.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh; Editing by Kirsten Donovan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-5-5T08:19:36.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200505eg5500xvh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
