\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russian rouble and equities gain on oil price recovery\b0\par\par\uc2 472 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 April 2020\par 16:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds OFZ bond auction result)\par \par \uc2 By Andrey Ostroukh and Alexander Marrow\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, April 22 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble pared early losses and firmed in volatile trade on Wednesday, pulling away from a three-week low hit in the previous trading session, as oil prices recovered from two-decade lows.\par \par \uc2 Russia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was supported by the finance ministry carrying out one of two planned OFZ treasury bond auctions, demand for which is usually seen as a gauge of investor sentiment towards Russian assets.\par \par \uc2 By 1428 GMT the rouble was up 1.2% against the dollar at 76.17 after weakening to 77.60 in early trade.\par \par \uc2 Against the euro, the rouble gained 1.4% to 82.57 , having briefly dropped to its weakest since early April of 84.27.\par \par \uc2 The rouble remains under pressure from the double-pronged threat of low oil prices and the coronavirus outbreak that is pushing the Russian economy into recession.\par \par \uc2 The price of benchmark Brent crude oil fell to its lowest since 1999 in early trade as global supply looks set to overwhelm demand for months to come, despite record production cuts agreed by \uc2 OPEC\uc2  and allies including Russia.\par \par \uc2 Later in the day, Brent futures were up 7.6% at $20.80 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 The correction in oil quotations and the general increase of risk appetite allowed the rouble to flourish on Wednesday, said Veles Capital analyst Yuri Kravchenko, adding that the rouble is coping relatively well with the collapse in oil prices.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  interest rate decision due on Friday is also in focus. Prices for OFZ bonds, which move inversely with their yields, rose this week on hopes for a rate cut.\par \par \uc2 The finance ministry enjoyed demand of 141 billion roubles ($1.85 billion) at its first OFZ auction of the day, but cancelled the second, citing a lack of bids at acceptable price levels.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is also supporting the rouble with daily sales of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from state reserves, \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's first \b \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since early 2015.\par \par \uc2 On Monday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  worth 16.8 billion roubles, up from 14.8 billion roubles on Friday and 12.9 billion roubles on Monday last week, its data showed on Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were responding well to the oil price rebound on Wednesday, with the rouble-based MOEX Russian index hitting a one-week high.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was up 4.7% to 1,059.4 points. The MOEX was 2.9% higher at 2,560.7 points.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 76.1400 roubles) (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh and Alexander Marrow; Editing by Larry King, David Goodman, William Maclean) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-4-22T15:41:58.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200422eg4m01cj9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
