\par\par \b \uc2 *S&PGR Affirms \uc2 Sogaz Insurance\uc2  At 'BBB'; Outlook Stable\b0\par\par\uc2 1,995 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 April 2020\par 13:18\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2020, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 6 Apr 2020 07:18 ET  Press Release: S&PGR Affirms \uc2 Sogaz Insurance\uc2  At 'BBB'; Outlook Stable\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  \par The following is a press release from S&P Global Ratings: \par  \par      -- On March 27, 2020, we revised the outlook on our local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating \par on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2   to negative reflecting our view of reduced headroom in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  's \par stand-alone credit metrics and continuing uncertainty in the global oil and \par gas markets. \par      -- We consider \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz Insurance\f28 \uc2 \f2  to be an equity investment of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2   and \par do not link our ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  to that on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  . \par      -- \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  has a sound capital cushion, leading position on the Russian \par insurance market, and a solid underwriting performance. \par      -- We are therefore affirming our 'BBB' ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 . \par      -- The stable outlook reflects our view that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  will sustain its \par business position and gradually strengthen its capital and earnings over the \par next two years. \par  \par MOSCOW (S&P Global Ratings) April 6, 2020--S&P Global Ratings today affirmed \par its 'BBB' long-term insurer financial strength and issuer credit ratings on \par Russia-based \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz Insurance\f28 \uc2 \f2 . The outlook is stable. \par  \par The affirmation follows the revision of our outlook on the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  \par rating on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2   to negative on March 27, 2020 (see "Lower Oil Prices Prompt \par Revision Of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  , \f28 \uc2 \f2 KazMunayGas\f28 \uc2 \f2  , And Tengizchevroil Outlooks To Negative"). \par At the same time, we consider that this situation doesn't have a direct and \par immediate impact on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 . Although \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2   owns 21.21% stake in \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  \par directly and via its subsidiaries, we view \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  as an equity investment and \par therefore do not link our ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  to that on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2  . This is because \par we consider that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  operates independently and financially, even though \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2   has some influence over \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  through its representation in the board \par and its status as one of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 's largest clients. In fact, \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  has multiple \par shareholders, including members of its management, which together own a 68.79% \par stake, and \f28 \uc2 \f2 VTB Bank\f28 \uc2 \f2   with 10%. This shareholding structure allows \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  to \par balance the interests of different stakeholders and its own strategic targets. \par  \par Given the current ownership structure, our main consideration related to \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 's projected dividend outflows, which we expect will comprise about 20% \par of its net profit in 2020-2021. In addition, we have not observed financial \par support for \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  from \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2   or any other shareholder in the past. This is \par because \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  remains financially independent and showed solid operating \par results in 2019 and earlier. \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  is also regulated by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of \par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Russia\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  , which makes it ring-fenced from potential negative \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from \par its owners. Consequently, we no longer regard \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  as a nonstrategic \par subsidiary of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Gazprom\f28 \uc2 \f2   and base our view of \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 's creditworthiness on its \par stand-alone characteristics. \par  \par We continue to consider \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 's leading positions in Russia, with solid \par margins underlying sound operating performance, a diversified premium base of \par corporate and retail clients, and sound risk profile. Moreover, regarding \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 's financial profile, we expect the company will gradually restore its \par capital adequacy after its acquisition of VTB Insurance, through retained \par earnings and its defined dividend policy. We consider that current \par developments on financial markets and the coronavirus pandemic will have no \par immediate impact on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 's growth prospects or bottom-line results. However, \par we acknowledge that a decline in business activity and intensifying \par competition can put some strain on further business development and \par underwriting performance. We also note that the current financial market \par turbulence can add volatility to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 's investment results. However, at the \par moment, we expect a limited impact since most of the invested assets are held \par to maturity. As the situation evolves, we will update our assumptions and \par estimates on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  accordingly. \par  \par We rate \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  above the related sovereign because we believe \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par consolidated balance sheet can withstand the potential impact of a \par hypothetical default of Russia. Under our foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sovereign stress \par scenario for Russia, we consider that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  would likely retain positive \par regulatory capital and maintain a liquidity ratio in excess of 100%. According \par to our criteria, this indicates that \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  is unlikely to default on its \par insurance liabilities under the scenario and therefore passes our sovereign \par foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stress test. Therefore, the ratings on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  can be one notch \par higher than our 'BBB-' long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating on Russia, but are \par limited by the 'BBB' long-term local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating on Russia due to \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2 's \par substantial business volumes in Russia. \par  \par The stable outlook on \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  reflects our view that the group will continue to \par advance its strategy to sustain its business position and gradually strengthen \par its capital and earnings over the next two years. We expect \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  can maintain \par its strong competitive position in the Russian insurance market, as well as \par its conservative investment policy. \par  \par We could lower the ratings in the next two years if, for instance: \par  \par      -- The group increased its exposure to lower-quality investments, or its \par capital position weakened, thereby undermining the group's ability to \par sustainably pass our hypothetical foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sovereign stress test; \par      -- Capital weakened for a prolonged period to below the 'BBB' level \par according to our capital model, squeezed either by a weaker operating \par performance than expected, investment losses, considerably higher dividend \par payouts, or expenditure for further acquisitions; or \par      -- We lowered our local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sovereign ratings on Russia. \par  \par A positive rating action is unlikely at this stage, given that the rating on \par \f28 \uc2 \f2 Sogaz\f28 \uc2 \f2  is at the level of the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sovereign rating. \par  \par RELATED CRITERIA \par  \par      -- Criteria | Insurance | General: Insurers Rating Methodology, July 1, \par 2019 \par      -- General Criteria: Group Rating Methodology, July 1, 2019 \par      -- General Criteria: Ratings Above The Sovereign--Corporate And \par Government Ratings: Methodology And Assumptions, Nov. 19, 2013 \par      -- Criteria | Insurance | General: Refined Methodology And Assumptions \par For Analyzing Insurer Capital Adequacy Using The Risk-Based Insurance Capital \par Model, June 7, 2010 \par      -- General Criteria: Use Of CreditWatch And Outlooks, Sept. 14, 2009 \par  \par Certain terms used in this report, particularly certain adjectives used to \par express our view on rating relevant factors, have specific meanings ascribed \par to them in our criteria, and should therefore be read in conjunction with such \par criteria. Please see Ratings Criteria at www.standardandpoors.com for further \par information. A description of each of S&P Global Ratings' rating categories is \par contained in "S&P Global Ratings Definitions" at \par  \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.standardandpoors.com/en_US/web/guest/article/-/view/sourceId/504352"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 https://www.standardandpoors.com/en_US/web/guest/article/-/view/sourceId/504352 }}}\uc2 \f2  \par Complete ratings information is available to subscribers of RatingsDir