\par\par \b \uc2 Russian rouble firms away from 80 vs dollar, stocks up\b0\par\par\uc2 452 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 10:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 31 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble firmed in volatile early trading on Tuesday, moving away from levels of 80 against the dollar hit the previous day when oil prices slid, while stock indexes inched higher.\par \par \uc2 At 0824 GMT, the rouble was 1.1% stronger against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 78.44, having hit 80.85 on Monday. It weakened to as much as 81.97 in mid-March, its worst performance since early 2016.\par \par \uc2 Versus the euro, the rouble gained 1.5% to 86.27 , moving away from Monday's low point of 89.11 and its weakest since early 2016 of 89.60 seen on March 19.\par \par \uc2 The rouble has lost more than 20% of its value so far this year {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/rngs/GLOBAL-CURRENCIES-PERFORMANCE/0100301V041/index.html"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://fingfx.thomsonreuters.com/gfx/rngs/GLOBAL-\b  \highlight22CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight22 -PERFORMANCE/0100301V041/index.html}}}\uc2  making it the worst-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar, as prices for oil, one of Russia's key exports, fell to multi-year lows.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, oil recovered some ground after U.S. President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  and Russian President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  agreed to talks to stabilise energy markets, with benchmarks climbing off 18-year lows hit as the coronavirus outbreak cut fuel demand worldwide.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was up 2.7% at $23.37 a barrel after falling as low as $21.65 on Monday.\par \par \uc2 If oil prices stay at such low levels in the coming days, the rouble may weaken beyond 80 against the dollar, said Dmitry Polevoy, chief economist at the \uc2 Russian Direct Investment Fund\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 From a technical analysis point of view, the dollar may see support at 77 roubles and resistance at 80, Alor Brokerage said in a note.\par \par \uc2 "But the current exchange rate is not a market one as relative stability of the rouble is the implication of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Alor said.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  started selling \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its reserves in March for the first time since early 2015 in an attempt to ease downside pressure on the rouble.\par \par \uc2 In the past few days, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was selling around 13.3 billion roubles ($168.76 million) worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  a day.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were higher. The dollar-denominated RTS index rose 4.4% to 1,000.9 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 2.4% higher at 2,491.9 points, well away from its all-time high of 3,226.89 hit in January.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see ($1 = 78.8080 roubles) (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh; Editing by Kirsten Donovan) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-3-31T09:27:41.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200331eg3v01hh1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
