\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 2-Russian rouble heads towards one-week high in volatile trade\b0\par\par\uc2 510 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 16:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 (Updates prices, adds U.S. jobless data, gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves)\par \par \uc2 By Alexander Marrow\par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 26 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble firmed against the dollar in volatile trade on Thursday, as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales helped outweigh concerns about low oil prices and the impact of the coronavirus outbreak.\par \par \uc2 The rouble reversed early losses and brushed aside record high unemployment data from the United States, as the market hoped for additional support measures from the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By 1525 GMT, the rouble was 1.2% stronger against the dollar at 77.31, heading towards a one-week high, and flat versus the euro, trading at 85.18.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was down 1.4% at $27.0 a barrel.\par \par \uc2 Weekly jobless claims in the United States surged to a record 3.28 million, higher than forecast, in another blow to the global economy, but the rouble was buoyed by \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales and exporting firms making monthly income tax payments.\par \par \uc2 The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued its \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , selling the equivalent of 13.4 billion roubles ($171.9 million)of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on March 24, taking its total sales to more than $1.1 billion in the past two weeks.\par \par \uc2 Russia's gold and \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves fell by $30 billion to $551.2 billion in just one week, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said, reflecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the regulator sought to halt the rouble's slide, which fell to four-year lows earlier this week.\par \par \uc2 Recorded coronavirus cases are beginning to rise more quickly in Russia, although the total of 840 is still far below the numbers in the United States and much of Europe.\par \par \uc2 The country said it would ground international flights from Friday and the mayor of Moscow said all restaurants, cafes, bars and shops, apart from those selling food and medicines, would close from March 28 until April 5.\par \par \uc2 Russia's budget can support new fiscal expenditures proposed by President \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  on Wednesday, Sofya Donets, chief economist at Renaissance Capital said, adding that growth would be hit if a newly-announced week-long holiday of workers was prolonged.\par \par \uc2 "We calculated our tentative scenario for this new reality with both domestic and external restrictions to be prolonged, and we see -0.8% y-o-y growth in Russia in 2020 in this scenario," she said.\par \par \uc2 ITI Capital's head of research Iskander Lutsko said Russia's gross domestic product (GDP) could decline around 0.15% in the short term.\par \par \uc2 Russian stock indexes were up.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was up 3.3% to 1,013.6 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 1.5% higher at 2,488.4 points.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see\par \par \uc2 ($1 = 77.9600 roubles) (Reporting by Alexander Marrow; additional reporting by Andrey Ostroukh; editing by Philippa Fletcher, Andrew Heavens and Toby Davis) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-3-26T16:36:06.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200326eg3q02jcx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwg