\par\par \b \uc2 Falling oil sends rouble towards lowest since early 2016, stocks down\b0\par\par\uc2 359 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2020\par 08:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2020 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 MOSCOW, March 23 (Reuters) - The Russian rouble eased on Monday, sliding towards its weakest levels since early 2016 amid falling oil prices and globally increasing fears about the coronavirus fallout.\par \par \uc2 The rouble shed 1.4% of its value to 81.04 versus the dollar as of 0711 GMT, trading near its weakest since late January 2016 of 81.97 it hit last Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Versus the euro, the rouble slid 1.9% to 87.04 .\par \par \uc2 The previous week became the worst one for the rouble since late 2014, when it saw a double-blast from falling oil prices and panic-fuelled demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  at home amid recently imposed financial and economic sanctions against Moscow.\par \par \uc2 Unlike in late 2014, when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised rates sharply to defend the rouble, last Friday it left its key rate unchanged at 6% last Friday, halting its monetary easing cycle.\par \par \uc2 Now, the U.S. dollar is playing the role of "defensive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 " at times of increasing market uncertainty related to the coronavirus, said Olma Brokerage.\par \par \uc2 Russia has registered 367 cases and one death resulting from the coronavirus, which has infected over 305,000 people worldwide and killed more than 13,000.\par \par \uc2 The rouble's downside is partially limited by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that started selling a limited amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  from its reserves this month, its first \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 2015.\par \par \uc2 Month-end taxes in \b \highlight22\uc2 Russia\b0 \highlight\uc2  should also cushion losses in the rouble as export-focused companies usually convert their \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues to meet local liabilities.\par \par \uc2 Brent crude oil, a global benchmark for Russia's main export, was down 3% at $26.18 a barrel, speaking for the downside pressure on Russian assets to last.\par \par \uc2 The dollar-denominated RTS index was down 5% to 878.2 points. The rouble-based MOEX Russian index was 3% lower at 2,259.7 points, heading away from its record high of 3,226.9 it high two months ago.\par \par \uc2 For Russian equities guide see\par \par \uc2 For Russian treasury bonds see (Reporting by Andrey Ostroukh; Editing by Toby Chopra) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2020-3-23T08:30:33.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020200323eg3n016z9\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Russia near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalph